msgstr "**Injektion af on- line script** Kollaps din JavaScript i en enkelt linje og injicerer det via `sub_filter` for minimalt fodaftryk og maksimal kompatibilitet."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Onion opt-in, not a port.** A category-keyed map of booleans naming which of the entity's own categories get a `HiddenServicePort` on the node onion. It declares no numbers: the port is read from `local` when the category is declared there and from `public` otherwise, matching what `container_ports` publishes. Collision detection ignores it."
msgstr "**Løg-ind, ikke en havn.** En kategoriseret kort over booster navngivning hvilken af virksomhedens egne kategorier får en `HiddenServicePort` på node løg. Det erklærer ingen numre: porten læses fra `local` når kategorien er angivet dér og fra `public` Ellers, matchende hvad `container_ports` publicerer. Kollision afslører det."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Onions, firewall and name resolution.** *svc-net-firewall* owns the packet filter as one nftables table per role. Tor carries mail to a .onion in both deploy modes, rejects forged sources on the guarded ports, and binds its dnsmasq listeners statically so a failed re-enumeration can no longer drop every one of them. The deployment declares its own address space once, the egress range moved out of the Docker pool, and the container resolver follows the live bridge instead of a guessed address. Every host-bound port requires an explicit onion decision. See [svc-net-firewall](roles/svc-net-firewall/README.md)."
msgstr "**Løg, firewall og navneopløsning.** *svc- net- firewall* ejer pakkefilteret som en nfstables tabel per rolle. Tor bærer mail til en .løg i begge implementere tilstande, afviser falske kilder på de bevogtede havne, og binder sine dnsmasq lyttere statisk, så en mislykket gentælling kan ikke længere slippe hver eneste af dem. Indsættelsen erklærer sin egen adresse plads én gang, egress rækkevidde flyttet ud af Docker pool, og container resolver følger den levende bro i stedet for en gættet adresse. Hver vært- bundet port kræver en udtrykkelig løg beslutning. Se [svc- net- firewall](roles/svc-net-firewall/README.md)."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Only bridging addons add a service block.** A `<target>:` service block is added to the row role ONLY for addons that declare a `bridges:` dependency (per Decision 3), i.e. the in-repo cross-role integrations; a plain addon with no cross-role dependency adds no service block. Each bridging addon's `<target>:` block carries the standard dynamic `enabled`/`shared` flags with matching true/false `meta/variants.yml` coverage, and (for web-facing pairs) a co-deploy Playwright spec. Across the in-repo ✅ set this is a bounded, mechanical expansion scoped to the bridging integrations, accepted as part of Decision 15's full scope."
msgstr "**Kun bro addons tilføje en service blok.** A `<target>:` service blok tilføjes til rækken rolle KUN for addons, der erklærer en `bridges:` afhængighed (pr. beslutning 3), dvs. in-repo cross-rolleintegration; en almindelig addon uden cross-rolleafhængighed tilføjer ingen service blok. Hver bro addons `<target>:` blok bærer standarddynamikken `enabled`/`shared` flag med matchende true / false `meta/variants.yml` dækning, og (til web- face par) en co-deployering Playwright spec. På tværs af in- repo ✅ sæt dette er en afgrænset, mekanisk ekspansion scoped til bridging integration, accepteret som en del af afgørelse 15er fuld rækkevidde."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Only the first start serves nothing.** The env is authoritative again on every start, so what `TOOL_SERVER_CONNECTIONS` carries is the state the container comes back with. Before any group exists that is a disabled entry, which is the safe direction: no access rather than every administrator. Once the provisioning task has created the group, its id lives in the token store, `vars/main.yml` reads it back on the next deploy, and the filter renders the entry enabled with its exact group grant. From then on a bare container restart restores a served, correctly scoped connection without a deploy."
msgstr "**Kun den første start tjener intet.** Env er autoritativ igen på hver start, så hvad `TOOL_SERVER_CONNECTIONS` bærer er den tilstand, beholderen kommer tilbage med. Før nogen gruppe findes, der er en deaktiveret indgang, som er den sikre retning: ingen adgang snarere end hver administrator. Når provisionsopgaven har skabt gruppen, bor dens id i token butikken, `vars/main.yml` læser det tilbage på den næste implementering, og filteret gør indgangen aktiveret med sin nøjagtige gruppe tilskud. Fra da af genstarter en bare container en serveret, korrekt opfanget forbindelse uden en implementering."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Only the first start serves nothing.** The env is authoritative again on every start, so what ``TOOL_SERVER_CONNECTIONS`` carries is the state the container comes back with. Before any group exists that is a disabled entry, which is the safe direction: no access rather than every administrator. Once the provisioning task has created the group, its id lives in the token store, ``vars/main.yml`` reads it back on the next deploy, and the filter renders the entry enabled with its exact group grant. From then on a bare container restart restores a served, correctly scoped connection without a deploy."
