# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via Keycloak:** configured automatically on first deploy."
msgstr "**SSO via Keycloak:** konfigureret automatisk ved første deployering."

# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via oauth2-proxy with auto-provisioning:** V1 gates all access through the shared Keycloak OIDC client (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty forwards the authenticated identity to n8n as a trusted `Remote-Email` header (`templates/proxy.conf.j2`); an `EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES` script (`files/hooks.js`, adapted from [PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso](https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso)) reads that header, auto-provisions a local n8n user on first sign-in, and issues n8n's own session cookie — so every Keycloak user lands directly in the workflow editor, with no second, n8n-local login step."
msgstr "**SSO via oauth2-proxy med automatisk hensættelse:** V1 porte al adgang gennem den delte Keycloak OIDC klient (oauth2-proxy- kant). openresty videresender den bekræftede identitet til n8n som en betroet `Remote-Email` header (`templates/proxy.conf.j2`); `EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES` script (`files/hooks.js`, tilpasset fra [PavelSozonov / n8n-community-sso](https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso)) læser, at header, auto- bestemmelser en lokal n8n bruger på første sign-in, og spørgsmål n8n 's egen session cookie - så hver Keycloak bruger lander direkte i workflow editor, med ingen sekund, n8n - lokal login trin."

# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via oauth2-proxy with auto-provisioning:** V1 gates all access through the shared Keycloak OIDC client (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty forwards the authenticated identity to n8n as a trusted ``Remote-Email`` header (``templates/proxy.conf.j2``); an ``EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES`` script (``files/hooks.js``, adapted from `PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso <https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso>`__) reads that header, auto-provisions a local n8n user on first sign-in, and issues n8n’s own session cookie — so every Keycloak user lands directly in the workflow editor, with no second, n8n-local login step."
msgstr "**SSO via oauth2-proxy med automatisk hensættelse:** V1 porte al adgang gennem den delte Keycloak OIDC klient (oauth2-proxy- kant). openresty videresender den bekræftede identitet til n8n som en betroet ``Remote-Email`` header (``templates/proxy.conf.j2``); ``EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES`` script (``files/hooks.js``, tilpasset fra `PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso <https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso>`__) læser, at header, auto- bestemmelser en lokal n8n bruger på første sign-in, og spørgsmål n8n 's egen session cookie - så hver Keycloak bruger lander direkte i workflow editor, med ingen sekund, n8n - lokal login trin."

# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO** is SuiteCRM's own SAML login against Keycloak (`sso.flavor: saml` in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml)), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall's SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to `/saml/acs` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak's realm descriptor by [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a `.onion` issuer is unresolvable directly. `/auth` stays reachable as the local break-glass login."
msgstr "**SSO** er SuiteCRMeget SAML-login mod Keycloak (`sso.flavor: saml` til [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml))Ikke en proxy foran det. Ubekræftede anmodninger ramte Symfoni firewall 's SAML indgang, som omdirigerer til Keycloak; påstanden kommer tilbage til `/saml/acs` og etablerer en reel SuiteCRM session, så app 'en gør sin egen autentificerede UI, herunder sin logout kontrol. Konti oprettes ved første login fra påstanden (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), og IdP underskrift certifikat læses fra Keycloak's realdeskriptor af [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) ved start, over Tor SOCKS proxy, når udsteder er et løg, fordi en `.onion` udsteder kan ikke løses direkte. `/auth` forbliver tilgængelig som den lokale break- glas login."

# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO** is SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak (``sso.flavor: saml`` in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall’s SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to ``/saml/acs`` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (``SAML_AUTO_CREATE``), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak’s realm descriptor by ```files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`` <./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh>`__ at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a ``.onion`` issuer is unresolvable directly. ``/auth`` stays reachable as the local break-glass login."
msgstr "**SSO** er SuiteCRM 's eget SAML-login mod Keycloak (``sso.flavor: saml`` til ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall’s SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to ``/saml/acs`` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (``SAML_AUTO_CREATE``), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak’s realm descriptor by ```files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`` <./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh>`__ at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a ``.onion`` issuer is unresolvable directly. ``/auth`` forbliver tilgængelig som den lokale break- glas login."

