# libretranslate
msgid "**The runtime identity differs.** act sets `ACT=true`, so `detect_gha_act()` in [runtime.py](../../../../utils/env/runtime.py) resolves `INFINITO_RUNNING_ON_GITHUB=false` where a real runner resolves `true`. Anything keyed off that fact behaves differently, and act cannot prove a fix to it either way."
msgstr "**Runtime identiteten er forskellig.** actionsæt `ACT=true`, så `detect_gha_act()` til [runtime.py](../../../../utils/env/runtime.py) resolves `INFINITO_RUNNING_ON_GITHUB=false` hvor en rigtig løber løser `true`. Alt, der keyed off at faktum opfører sig anderledes, og handle kan ikke bevise en rettelse til det enten måde."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The seal key is the whole ballgame.** The ``static`` seal wraps the raft root key with ``secrets.credentials.seal_key``, injected as ``env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY``. A backup of the raft volume is **undecryptable without it**, and ``svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`` does not cover it — the encrypted inventory is its only home, so back the inventory up accordingly. It is pinned ``rotatable: false``: the static seal carries one generation of slack, and spending that every deploy makes any skipped generation unrecoverable. Rotate it deliberately by changing the inventory value; ``openbao.hcl.j2`` then emits the ``previous_key``/``previous_key_id`` pair, the node unseals with the old key and rewraps to the new one."
msgstr "**Seglnøglen er hele kampen.** Den ``static`` segl wraps tømmerrodnøglen med ``secrets.credentials.seal_key``, injiceret som ``env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY``. En backup af tømmerflåden volumen er **undecryptable uden det**, og ``svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`` dækker det ikke - den krypterede beholdning er dens eneste hjem, så tilbage fortegnelsen op i overensstemmelse hermed. Den sidder fast ``rotatable: false``: den statiske segl bærer en generation af slæk, og udgifter, som hver implementering gør enhver sprunget generation uinddrivelig. Rotere det bevidst ved at ændre lagerværdien; ``openbao.hcl.j2`` derefter udsender ``previous_key``/``previous_key_id`` par, knude unseal med den gamle nøgle og rewraps til den nye."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The seal key is the whole ballgame.** The `static` seal wraps the raft root key with `secrets.credentials.seal_key`, injected as `env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY`. A backup of the raft volume is **undecryptable without it**, and `svc-bkp-secrets-2-local` does not cover it — the encrypted inventory is its only home, so back the inventory up accordingly. It is pinned `rotatable: false`: the static seal carries one generation of slack, and spending that every deploy makes any skipped generation unrecoverable. Rotate it deliberately by changing the inventory value; `openbao.hcl.j2` then emits the `previous_key`/`previous_key_id` pair, the node unseals with the old key and rewraps to the new one."
msgstr "**Seglnøglen er hele kampen.** Den `static` segl wraps tømmerrodnøglen med `secrets.credentials.seal_key`, injiceret som `env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY`. En backup af tømmerflåden volumen er **undecryptable uden det**, og `svc-bkp-secrets-2-local` dækker det ikke - den krypterede beholdning er dens eneste hjem, så tilbage fortegnelsen op i overensstemmelse hermed. Den sidder fast `rotatable: false`: den statiske segl bærer en generation af slæk, og udgifter, som hver implementering gør enhver sprunget generation uinddrivelig. Rotere det bevidst ved at ændre lagerværdien; `openbao.hcl.j2` derefter udsender `previous_key`/`previous_key_id` par, knude unseal med den gamle nøgle og rewraps til den nye."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The version has to fit.** The dump states which server it came out of, in its own header — `-- Dumped from database version 17.11` for postgres, `-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB` for mariadb. That is compared against the running engine before the pre-clean touches anything. Restoring forward across a major version is the upgrade path and stays allowed; backward is refused, because a newer dump uses syntax an older server rejects and the schema would already be dropped by then. The version is deliberately not kept in `databases.csv`: that file is written at seed time and would state the version deployed back then, not the one the dump came from — and a generation copied to another host carries its header along, a csv row does not."
msgstr "**Versionen skal passe.** Den dump stater hvilken server det kom ud af, i sin egen header - `-- Dumped from database version 17.11` for postgres `-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB` for mariadb. Det sammenlignes med den kørende motor, før den rensede rører noget. Gendannelse frem på tværs af en større version er opgraderingsstien og forbliver tilladt; baglæns afvises, fordi en nyere dump bruger syntaks en ældre server afviser og skemaet ville allerede blive droppet inden da. Den er bevidst ikke holdt i `databases.csv`: denne fil er skrevet ved seed time og ville angive den version, der blev indsat dengang, ikke den, dump kom fra - og en generation kopieret til en anden vært bærer sin overskrift langs, en csv række ikke."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The version has to fit.** The dump states which server it came out of, in its own header — ``-- Dumped from database version 17.11`` for postgres, ``-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB`` for mariadb. That is compared against the running engine before the pre-clean touches anything. Restoring forward across a major version is the upgrade path and stays allowed; backward is refused, because a newer dump uses syntax an older server rejects and the schema would already be dropped by then. The version is deliberately not kept in ``databases.csv``: that file is written at seed time and would state the version deployed back then, not the one the dump came from — and a generation copied to another host carries its header along, a csv row does not."
msgstr "**Versionen skal passe.** Den dump stater hvilken server det kom ud af, i sin egen header - ``-- Dumped from database version 17.11`` for postgres ``-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB`` for mariadb. Det sammenlignes med den kørende motor, før den rensede rører noget. Gendannelse frem på tværs af en større version er opgraderingsstien og forbliver tilladt; baglæns afvises, fordi en nyere dump bruger syntaks en ældre server afviser og skemaet ville allerede blive droppet inden da. Den er bevidst ikke holdt i ``databases.csv``: denne fil er skrevet ved seed time og ville angive den version, der blev indsat dengang, ikke den, dump kom fra - og en generation kopieret til en anden vært bærer sin overskrift langs, en csv række ikke."

