# libretranslate
msgid "As a Infinito.Nexus platform operator, I want to provide a fully integrated, production-ready Penpot design and prototyping platform within the Infinito.Nexus ecosystem so that teams can create, collaborate on, and share design projects directly inside their sovereign Infinito.Nexus installation."
msgstr "Som en Infinito.Nexus platform operatør, jeg ønsker at give en fuldt integreret, produktion-klar Penpot design og prototyping platform inden for Infinito.Nexus økosystem, så teams kan skabe, samarbejde om og dele designprojekter direkte inden for deres suveræne Infinito.Nexus installation."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a client, each managed MCP Client Tool node MUST use Bearer or Header authentication and an explicit include list. The upstream `include: all` behavior MUST NOT be used for deployment-managed workflows."
msgstr "Som en klient, hver administrerede MCP Client Tool node SKAL bruge Bearer eller Header godkendelse og en eksplicit omfatte liste. Opstrøms `include: all` adfærd SKAL IKKE bruges til deployeringsstyrede arbejdsgange."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a contributor maintaining the per-role Playwright suite, I want every role whose `meta/services.yml` declares `ldap.enabled` (literal `true` or the dynamic `\"{{ 'svc-db-openldap' in group_names }}\"` form) to ship a Playwright scenario that exercises the LDAP-bind login path end-to-end, so that the LDAP variant of the role's authentication stack is verified independently from its OIDC counterpart."
msgstr "Som bidragyder til at opretholde rollen Playwright suite, Jeg ønsker enhver rolle, hvis `meta/services.yml` erklærer `ldap.enabled` (bogstaveligt `true` eller dynamikken `\"{{ 'svc-db-openldap' in group_names }}\"` form) at sende en Playwright scenario, der udøver LDAP-bind login sti end-to-end, således at LDAP variant af rollens godkendelse stak er verificeret uafhængigt af sin OIDC modstykke."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a contributor maintaining the per-role Playwright suite, I want every role whose login flow is RBAC-gated (OIDC and/or LDAP) to also exercise the canonical non-admin user `biber` end-to-end, so that the RBAC plumbing from [004 - Generic RBAC role auto-provisioning](README.md#archive) is verified per role rather than only on the privileged-admin path."
msgstr "Som en bidragyder opretholde per- rolle Playwright suite, Jeg vil have hver rolle, hvis login flow er RBAC-gated (OIDC og / eller LDAP) at også udøve den kanoniske ikke-admin bruger `biber` ende-til-ende, så RBAC VVS fra [004 - Generisk RBAC rolle auto- hensættelse](README.md#archive) er verificeret per rolle snarere end kun på admin sti."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a contributor to Infinito.Nexus, I want every role that ships application-level extensions to declare them through one unified `meta/addons/` contract (one file per addon), instead of today's per-app spelling (`addons`, `plugins`, `extensions`, `modules`, `mu_plugins`) scattered across `meta/services.yml`, `vars/main.yml`, and `tasks/`, so that addons are discoverable, lintable, and testable with a single schema, and so that any addon that bridges into another role declares that dependency explicitly through a service flag in `meta/services.yml`."
msgstr "Som bidragyder til Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil have enhver rolle, at skibe ansøgning-niveau udvidelser til at erklære dem gennem en samlet `meta/addons/` kontrakt (én fil pr. addon), i stedet for dagens per- app stavning (`addons`, `plugins`, `extensions`, `modules`, `mu_plugins`) spredt over `meta/services.yml`, `vars/main.yml`, og `tasks/`, således at addons er lokaliserbare, literable, og testable med et enkelt skema, og således at enhver addon, der broer til en anden rolle erklærer, at afhængighed udtrykkeligt gennem en service flag i `meta/services.yml`."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a contributor, I want a requirements template so that new requirements are consistent and machine-readable."
msgstr "Som bidragyder ønsker jeg en kravskabelon, så nye krav er konsistente og maskinlæsbare."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a developer, I want to run the Infinito.Nexus CI on a dedicated server so that the deploy + test cycle is no longer bound by local hardware restrictions."
msgstr "Som udvikler, Jeg ønsker at køre Infinito.Nexus CI på en dedikeret server, så implementeringscyklussen + testcyklussen ikke længere er bundet af lokale hardwarebegrænsninger."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a maintainer of Infinito.Nexus, I want every user-facing string that core ships extracted into gettext catalogs and machine-translated by LibreTranslate through `make`, so that the API, the documentation and every consumer app serve all ISO 639-1 languages from one source of truth in this repository."
msgstr "Som vedligeholder af Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil have alle bruger- vender streng, der kerne skibe udvindes til gettext kataloger og maskiner- oversat af LibreTranslate gennem `make`, således at API, dokumentationen og hver forbruger app tjene alle ISO 639-1 sprog fra en sandhedskilde i dette arkiv."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want ERPNext (Frappe Framework) integrated as a `web-app-erpnext` role with OpenID Connect identity provider integration so that users can access the ERP through the same Single Sign-On (SSO) mechanism used across the Infinito.Nexus ecosystem, reusing the platform's central database and cache services."
msgstr "Som en platform administrator af Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil have ERPNext (Frappe Framework) integreret som en `web-app-erpnext` rolle med OpenID Connect identitet udbyder integration, så brugerne kan få adgang til ERP gennem den samme Single Sign-On (SSO) mekanisme anvendt på tværs af Infinito.Nexus økosystem, genbruge platformens centrale database og cache-tjenester."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want [Checkmk](https://github.com/Checkmk/checkmk) integrated as a `web-app-checkmk` role with Keycloak SSO (via the oauth2-proxy gate) and native LDAP user management so that operators can run the open-source Checkmk monitoring server behind the platform's central Single Sign-On, validated end-to-end with Playwright personas."
msgstr "Som en platform administrator af Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil have [CheckmkComment](https://github.com/Checkmk/checkmk) integreret som en `web-app-checkmk` rolle med Keycloak SSO (via oauth2-proxy- gate) og native LDAP-brugerstyring, så operatørerne kan køre open-source Checkmk overvågning server bag platformens centrale Single Sign-On, valideret end-to-end med Playwright personas."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want [Jellyfin](https://jellyfin.org) integrated as a `web-app-jellyfin` role with Keycloak-backed Single Sign-On so that users can stream the media server behind the platform's central identity, validated end-to-end with Playwright personas."
msgstr "Som en platform administrator af Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil have [Jellyfin Formand](https://jellyfin.org) integreret som en `web-app-jellyfin` rolle med Keycloak- bakkes Single Sign-On, så brugerne kan streame medieserveren bag platformens centrale identitet, valideret end-to-end med Playwright personas."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want [Semaphore UI](https://github.com/semaphoreui/semaphore) integrated as a `web-app-semaphore` role with OpenID Connect (Keycloak) SSO and optional LDAP login so that operators can run Ansible / Terraform / OpenTofu / Bash automation from a web UI behind the platform's central Single Sign-On, reusing the central database, and validated end-to-end with Playwright personas."
msgstr "Som en platform administrator af Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil have [Semaphore UI](https://github.com/semaphoreui/semaphore) integreret som en `web-app-semaphore` rolle med OpenID Connect (Keycloak) SSO og valgfri LDAP login, så operatørerne kan køre Ansible / Terraform / OpenTofu / Bash automatisering fra en web UI bag platformens centrale Single Sign-On, genbruge den centrale database, og valideret end-to-end med Playwright personas."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want a `svc-ai-robot` role that turns one dedicated machine into an embodied platform for Hermes, giving the agent scoped-to-full host access so it can explore its own hardware and act in the physical world, so that Hermes can \"come to life\" on a robot while this power stays confined to a dedicated, segmented device and never leaks onto shared infrastructure."
msgstr "Som en platform administrator af Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil have en `svc-ai-robot` rolle, der gør en dedikeret maskine til en legemliggjort platform for Hermes, giver agent scoped- to- fuld vært adgang, så det kan udforske sin egen hardware og handle i den fysiske verden, så Hermes kan \"komme til live\" på en robot, mens denne kraft forbliver begrænset til en dedikeret, segmenteret enhed og aldrig lækker på delt infrastruktur."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want a `web-app-homeassistant` role that deploys [Home Assistant](https://www.home-assistant.io/) and exposes its native MCP server, so that agent employees (Hermes on a Pi, [032](032-agent-employees-firecracker.md)) and other MCP clients can control home devices as scoped MCP tools without any host access, making the \"isolated home assistant\" scenario concrete."
msgstr "Som en platform administrator af Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil have en `web-app-homeassistant` rolle, der anvender [Home Assistant](https://www.home-assistant.io/) og udsætter sin indfødte MCP server, så agent medarbejdere (Hermes på en Pi, [032](032-agent-employees-firecracker.md)) og andre MCP klienter kan styre hjem enheder som scoped MCP værktøjer uden nogen vært adgang, hvilket gør \"isoleret hjemmeassistent\" konkrete scenarier."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want a self-hostable `web-app-atmo` role that deploys an [atmo.rsvp](https://atmo.rsvp) instance (upstream [flo-bit/atmo-events](https://github.com/flo-bit/atmo-events), the successor to OpenMeet) wired to the platform's existing AT Protocol identity, and a bridge that mirrors calendar events between AT Protocol and Mobilizon, so that events created on my instance appear simultaneously on the AT Protocol (Bluesky) network and the ActivityPub (Fediverse) network from a single source of truth."
msgstr "Som en platform administrator af Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil have en selv- hostable `web-app-atmo` rolle, der implementerer en [atmo.rsvp](https://atmo.rsvp) instans (opstrøms [floot- bit / atmosfærehændelser](https://github.com/flo-bit/atmo-events), efterfølgeren til OpenMeet) forbundet til platformens eksisterende ATProtocol identitet, og en bro, der afspejler kalenderbegivenheder mellem AT Protocol og Mobilizon, så begivenheder skabt på min instans vises samtidigt på AT-protokollen (Bluesky) netværk og ActivityPub (Fediverse) netværk fra en enkelt sandhedskilde."

msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want a single OpenAI-compatible LLM gateway that routes to any model backend (local Ollama, LM Studio, OpenRouter, ...), so that every AI consumer (OpenWebUI, Flowise, and the agent employees in [032](032-agent-employees-firecracker.md)) targets one `/v1` endpoint and I swap or add model backends centrally without touching any consumer."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want every role with a documented Model Context Protocol (MCP) surface to expose or consume MCP through the platform's standard service, identity, proxy, and test contracts so that AI clients can use application data and actions safely without one-off per-role wiring."
msgstr "Som en platform administrator af Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil have hver rolle med en dokumenteret model kontekstprotokol (MCP) overflade til at afsløre eller forbruge MCP gennem platformens standard service, identitet, proxy og test kontrakter, så AI-klienter kan bruge applikationsdata og handlinger sikkert uden one-off perrolleledninger."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want every role with an `application_id` to have an explicit, evidence-based MCP disposition and every suitable application to expose a narrowly curated MCP surface to Open WebUI, Flowise, n8n, and other approved clients so that applications can be connected without turning shared administrator credentials, raw infrastructure APIs, or arbitrary network access into agent tools."
msgstr "Som en platform administrator af Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil have hver rolle med en `application_id` at have en eksplicit, bevisbaseret MCP disposition og alle passende program til at afsløre en snævert kureret MCP overflade til Open WebUI, Flowise, n8n, og andre godkendte kunder, således at applikationer kan tilsluttes uden at vende delte administratoroplysninger, rå infrastruktur API 'er, eller vilkårlig netværksadgang til agent værktøjer."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want the `web-app-matrix` role to gain a second deployment flavor that delegates the heavy lifting to the upstream [matrix-docker-ansible-deploy](https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy) (MDAD) playbook, so that the full Matrix ecosystem — Synapse, Element, every supported bridge, Jitsi-backed video conferencing, ma1sd / Dimension / hookshot / etcetera — is available without the role re-implementing each service from scratch. The existing role-internal compose stack stays selectable as the `compose` flavor for one cycle, marked deprecated."
msgstr "Som en platform administrator af Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil have `web-app-matrix` rolle til at få en anden implementering smag, der uddelegerer tunge løft til opstrøms [matrix- docker- ansible- deployering](https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy) (MDAD) afspilningsbog, så den fulde Matrix økosystem - Synapse, Element, hver understøttet bro, Jitsi- bakkes video konference, ma1sd / Dimension / hookshot / etctera - er tilgængelig uden rollen re- implementere hver service fra bunden. Den eksisterende role- interne komponentstak forbliver valgbar som `compose` Smagen til en cyklus, mærket forældet."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want to deploy self-hostable AI agent platforms (Hermes Agent, OpenClaw) as kernel-isolated, scalable \"employees\" across my nodes, coordinated by a Flowise supervisor over MCP and routed to models through the [031](031-llm-gateway-model-backends.md) gateway, so that I run a fleet of isolated agents with cross-agent pipelines and kernel-level isolation, without bespoke per-agent wiring."
msgstr "Som en platform administrator af Infinito.Nexus, Jeg ønsker at indsætte selv- hostable AI agent platforme (Hermes Agent, OpenClaw) som kernel- isoleret, skalerbar \"employees\" på tværs af mine knudepunkter, koordineret af en Flowise vejleder over MCP og dirigeret til modeller gennem [031](031-llm-gateway-model-backends.md) Gateway, så jeg kører en flåde af isolerede agenter med krydsagtige rørledninger og kernelniveau isolering, uden skræddersyede peragent ledninger."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator, I want Infinito.Nexus to support multi-node Docker Swarm deployments with NFS-backed shared volumes, so that services can be rescheduled across nodes without losing persistent data, scaled horizontally, and updated with rolling updates — gaining high availability without introducing Kubernetes complexity."
msgstr "Som en platform administrator, jeg ønsker Infinito.Nexus at støtte multi- node Docker Swarm implementeringer med NFS- støttede delte mængder, så tjenester kan omlægges på tværs af knudepunkter uden at miste vedvarende data, skaleres vandret, og opdateres med rullende opdateringer - få høj tilgængelighed uden at indføre Kubernetes kompleksitet."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a self-hoster running Infinito.Nexus behind NAT/CGNAT/dynamic IP (Raspberry Pi, edge node, home server), I want a `svc-net-tor` role that makes the node's primary domain a Tor v3 `.onion` address so that the entire stack (web, SSO, LDAP, CA) is reachable over Tor without public IP, port forwarding, VPS, or DynDNS — while individual apps can still attach extra public domains with their own TLS."
msgstr "Som self-hoster kører Infinito.Nexus bag NAT/CGNAT/dynamic IP (Raspberry Pi, kant knude, home server), Jeg vil have en `svc-net-tor` rolle, der gør node 's primære domæne en Tor v3 `.onion` adresse, så hele stakken (web, SSO, LDAP, CA) er tilgængelig over Tor uden offentlig IP, port videresendelse, VPS, eller DynDNS - mens individuelle apps kan stadig vedhæfte ekstra offentlige domæner med deres egne TLS."

# libretranslate
msgid "As a server, each managed MCP Server Trigger workflow MUST:"
msgstr "Som server skal hver enkelt styret MCP Server Trigger-arbejdsgang:"

# libretranslate
msgid "As a visitor of an Infinito.Nexus deployment, I want the documentation, the universal logout panel and the dashboard to speak my language from the core gettext catalogs, and I want browser apps such as MIG to be allowed to read the API, so that every surface core renders follows the same translations."
msgstr "Som besøgende af en Infinito.Nexus implementering, Jeg vil have dokumentation, den universelle logout panel og dashboard til at tale mit sprog fra kernen gettext kataloger, og jeg vil have browser apps som MIG at få lov til at læse API, så hver overflade kerne gør følger de samme oversættelser."

# libretranslate
msgid "As an Infinito.Nexus administrator, I want [OpenBao](https://github.com/openbao/openbao) deployed as a `web-app-openbao` role with Keycloak OIDC login, group-mapped policies, persistent storage, automatic unsealing, backup and monitoring, so that infrastructure secrets, application credentials, certificates and tokens can be stored and retrieved centrally without distributing static secrets across systems."
msgstr "Som en Infinito.Nexus administrator, jeg vil have [OpenBao](https://github.com/openbao/openbao) anvendes som en `web-app-openbao` rolle med Keycloak OIDC login, group- mapped politikker, vedvarende opbevaring, automatisk afforsegling, backup og overvågning, så infrastruktur hemmeligheder, ansøgning legitimation, certifikater og tokens kan gemmes og hentes centralt uden at distribuere statiske hemmeligheder på tværs af systemer."

# libretranslate
