# libretranslate
msgid "Both helpers degrade gracefully:"
msgstr "Begge hjælpere fornedrer yndefuldt:"

# libretranslate
msgid "Both journeys are covered bespoke in ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``, which targets the ``openid-connect/auth`` href explicitly, opens ``/admin``, and signs out at ``/admin/ui/logout``; a second scenario drives the biber-to-administrator mail round-trip across two browser contexts. The path back to the generic personas is a distinguishable login control on Mailu’s SSO page."
msgstr "Begge rejser er dækket skræddersyet i ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``, der er rettet mod ``openid-connect/auth`` Forklar udtrykkeligt, åbner ``/admin``, og tegn ud på ``/admin/ui/logout``; et andet scenario driver biber- to- administrator mail rundtur på tværs af to browser-sammenhænge. Vejen tilbage til den generiske personas er en skelnen login kontrol på Mailu s SSO side."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both journeys are covered bespoke in ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``: the master-realm super administrator drives the admin console, and the normal-realm administrator and biber each drive the realm account console including sign-out. The path back to the generic personas is an app-shaped surface behind the shared auth chain, which the identity provider by definition does not have."
msgstr "Begge rejser er dækket skræddersyet i ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``: den mester- rige super administrator driver admin konsol, og den normale-rige administrator og biber hver kører den rige konto konsol herunder sign-out. Vejen tilbage til de generiske personas er en app- formet overflade bag den fælles auth kæde, som den identitet udbyder per definition ikke har."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both journeys are covered bespoke in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`, which targets the `openid-connect/auth` href explicitly, opens `/admin`, and signs out at `/admin/ui/logout`; a second scenario drives the biber-to-administrator mail round-trip across two browser contexts. The path back to the generic personas is a distinguishable login control on Mailu's SSO page."
msgstr "Begge rejser er dækket skræddersyet i `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`, der er rettet mod `openid-connect/auth` Forklar udtrykkeligt, åbner `/admin`, og tegn ud på `/admin/ui/logout`; et andet scenario driver biber- to- administrator mail rundtur på tværs af to browser-sammenhænge. Vejen tilbage til den generiske personas er en skelnen login kontrol på Mailu s SSO side."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both journeys are covered bespoke in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`: the master-realm super administrator drives the admin console, and the normal-realm administrator and biber each drive the realm account console including sign-out. The path back to the generic personas is an app-shaped surface behind the shared auth chain, which the identity provider by definition does not have."
msgstr "Begge rejser er dækket skræddersyet i `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`: den mester- rige super administrator driver admin konsol, og den normale-rige administrator og biber hver kører den rige konto konsol herunder sign-out. Vejen tilbage til de generiske personas er en app- formet overflade bag den fælles auth kæde, som den identitet udbyder per definition ikke har."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both layers are process-wide in-process caches. They intentionally do NOT track on-disk file mtimes; CLI tools are short-lived and the assumption \"the on-disk file does not change while my process runs\" holds. The single exception is `utils.cache.yaml.dump_yaml`, which writes through and evicts the cached entry for the path it just wrote so a tool that edits a file mid-run sees the new content on the next read."
msgstr "Begge lag er proces- brede procescache. De bevidst ikke spore on- disk fil mtimes; CLI værktøjer er kortlivede og antagelse \"On- disk filen ændrer sig ikke, mens min proces kører\" holder. Den eneste undtagelse er: `utils.cache.yaml.dump_yaml`, som skriver igennem og udskriver den cachede indgang for den sti, det lige skrev, så et værktøj, der redigerer en fil mid- run ser det nye indhold på den næste læse."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both need the same facts about a role: whether it ships its own container stack, and which deploy modes it supports. Keeping the logic here means the two callers never drift."
msgstr "Begge har brug for de samme fakta om en rolle: om det skibe sin egen container stak, og som implementere modes det understøtter. At holde logikken her betyder, at de to ringer aldrig driver."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both on the position"
msgstr "Begge på positionen"

# libretranslate
msgid "Both paths elevate privileges via `sudo` when not run as root, and the script verifies `bwrap` and `socat` on `PATH` before it exits. macOS uses `sandbox-exec` from the base system and does not need this target."
msgstr "Begge veje hæve privilegier via `sudo` når du ikke kører som root, og scriptet verificerer `bwrap` og `socat` om `PATH` før den kommer ud. macOS-anvendelser `sandbox-exec` fra basissystemet og ikke har brug for dette mål."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both platforms run model-generated code, which is untrusted, so a kernel-level boundary is required on top of their in-app sandboxing. [gVisor](https://gvisor.dev/) provides that boundary behind an OCI runtime, so each agent app stays a normal container spec and only pins `runtime: runsc`, reusing the existing image pipeline, replicas, healthchecks, and dual-mode machinery. [Kata Containers](https://katacontainers.io/) wrapping Firecracker was the original choice; Decision #2 records why it is unreachable on this container engine. ([E2B](https://github.com/e2b-dev/infra) is the higher-level alternative but brings its own Nomad/Consul orchestration and x86-cloud self-host, which would replace the swarm model.)"
msgstr "Begge platforme kører modelgenereret kode, som er utroværdig, så en kernel- niveau grænse er påkrævet på toppen af deres in-app sandboksning. [gVisor](https://gvisor.dev/) giver denne grænse bag en OCI runtime, så hver agent app forbliver en normal container spec og kun pins `runtime: runsc`, genbruge den eksisterende billed pipeline, kopier, sundhedstjek, og dualmode maskiner. [Kata Containers](https://katacontainers.io/) indpakning Firecracker var det oprindelige valg; Decision #2 registrerer, hvorfor den ikke kan nås på denne containermotor. ([DK2B](https://github.com/e2b-dev/infra) er det højere niveau alternativ, men bringer sin egen Nomad / Consul orkester og x86-cloud self-host, som ville erstatte sværmmodellen.)"

# libretranslate
msgid "Both pools feed the assignment, so narrowing `distros` to one value pins every row to it rather than reducing the run."
msgstr "Begge pools fodrer opgaven, så indsnævring `distros` til en værdi pins hver række til det i stedet for at reducere løbeturen."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both renderers fail loudly when Jinja markers cannot be resolved so generated configs never silently leak unrendered placeholders."
msgstr "Begge gengivere fejler højt, når Jinja markører ikke kan løses, så genererede config aldrig lydløst lække undereted pladsholdere."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both requirement files name the same collections at the same versions: the Galaxy file is the normal source, the git file the fallback used when galaxy.ansible.com is unreachable. A bump that touches only one of them would make the fallback install something the pin does not describe, so an update is applied to both or to neither."
msgstr "Begge krav filer navngiver de samme samlinger på de samme versioner: Galaxy-filen er den normale kilde, git-filen fallback bruges, når galaxy.ansible.com er uopnåelig. En bump, der rører kun én af dem ville gøre fallback installere noget, stiften ikke beskriver, så en opdatering anvendes på begge eller ingen af dem."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both run from the trusted workflow ref and check out the version tag for the actual build payload, so the release artefacts match the tagged commit byte-for-byte."
msgstr "Begge køre fra den betroede workflow ref og tjekke version tag for den faktiske bygge nyttelast, så udgivelsen artefacts matcher den mærkede commit byte- for- byte."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both sides pass `primary_apps` (not the round closure) as the BFS seed and the variant-merged services map for that round, so the reachability walk sees the same topology the inventory baked."
msgstr "Begge sider passerer `primary_apps` (ikke den runde lukning) som BFS frø og variant- fusionerede tjenester kort for denne runde, så nåelighed gå ser den samme topologi lageret bagt."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both sources carry the same pinned collections, so the only thing separating them is how long they take and whether they answer at all. A single slow day says nothing: galaxy.ansible.com degrades and recovers, and a git clone can stall on one runner. The default is therefore retuned only when a rolling window of daily samples shows one source durably behind the other."
msgstr "Begge kilder bærer de samme faste samlinger, så det eneste, der adskiller dem, er, hvor lang tid de tager, og om de overhovedet svarer. En eneste langsom dag siger intet: galaxy.ansible.com nedbryder og genvinder, og en git klon kan holde på én løber. Standard er derfor kun retuned, når en rullende vindue af daglige prøver viser den ene kilde varigt bag den anden."

# libretranslate
#, no-python-format
msgid "Both targets (Debian changelog and the RPM ``%changelog`` section) are fully regenerated on every run from the kept entries plus an archived-releases notice that points at the documentation site and lists the archived versions and dates as plain text. The notice is folded into the body of the oldest kept entry (not appended after the last entry), because free text after the final entry is not valid changelog data and makes the native parsers warn. Because the package files are regenerated, they cannot drift from the CHANGELOG.md SPOT."
msgstr "Begge mål (Debian changelog og RPM ``%changelog`` Afsnit) er fuldt regenereret på hvert løb fra de bevarede poster plus en arkivudgivelser varsel, der peger på dokumentation site og viser de arkiverede versioner og datoer som almindelig tekst. Meddelelsen er foldet ind i kroppen af den ældste holdt adgang (ikke vedlagt efter den sidste angivelse), fordi fri tekst efter den endelige indgang er ikke gyldig changelog data og gør de indfødte parsers advare. Fordi pakkefilerne regenereres, kan de ikke drive fra CHANGELOG.md SPOT."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both terms (application_id, service_key) are required."
msgstr "Begge udtryk (application_id, service_key) er påkrævet."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both terms (application_id, service_key) are required. ``services.<service_key>.name`` must exist in the resolved application config."
msgstr "Begge udtryk (application_id, service_key) er påkrævet. ``services.<service_key>.name`` skal eksistere i den løste applikationskonfiguration."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both terms (application_id, service_key) are required. ``services.<service_key>.name`` must exist in the resolved application config; the stack name is derived from ``application_id`` via the ``get_entity_name`` filter (matching how ``docker stack deploy`` names the stack in ``sys-svc-compose/handlers/main.yml``)."
msgstr "Begge udtryk (application_id, service_key) er påkrævet. ``services.<service_key>.name`` skal findes i den løste applikationskonfig; staknavnet er afledt af ``application_id`` via ``get_entity_name`` filter (matchende hvordan ``docker stack deploy`` navngiver stakken i ``sys-svc-compose/handlers/main.yml``)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both terms (application_id, service_key) are required; they are validated by `image`."
msgstr "Begge udtryk (application_id, service_key) er påkrævet; de valideres af `image`."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both tests route every read through the project caches (`utils.cache.files`, `utils.cache.yaml`); contributors adding a new variable scanner MUST do the same instead of calling `yaml.safe_load*` or `open()` directly."
msgstr "Begge tests rute hver læse gennem projektet cache (`utils.cache.files`, `utils.cache.yaml`); bidragydere der tilføjer en ny variabel scanner SKAL gøre det samme i stedet for at ringe `yaml.safe_load*` eller `open()` direkte."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both the CLI that parses ``--set`` and the inventory manager that consumes the parsed pairs build the key here, so a credential is addressed by exactly one string. A short form would name different credentials on different apps."
msgstr "Begge de CLI, der parser ``--set`` og lagerhåndtering, der forbruger de parrede par bygge nøglen her, så en kredit er behandlet af præcis én streng. En kort form ville navngive forskellige akkreditiver på forskellige apps."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both the role-meta lint (`tests/lint/ansible/services/test_addons_schema.py`) and the opt-in external drift checker (`tests/external/update/addons/`) read the constants here so the two layers never drift apart: the lint validates that an addon's declared `mechanism`/`source`/`update.catalog` is one the checker actually understands, and the checker only walks catalogs it has an adapter for."
msgstr "Begge dele (`tests/lint/ansible/services/test_addons_schema.py`) og opt- i ekstern driftskontrol (`tests/external/update/addons/`) læse konstanterne her, så de to lag aldrig glider fra hinanden: linten validerer, at en addon er erklæret `mechanism`/`source`/`update.catalog` er en den checker faktisk forstår, og checker kun går kataloger det har en adapter til."

# libretranslate
msgid "Bounding a service port that carries no access policy of its own, where the packet filter is the only boundary available."
msgstr "Bounding en service port, der bærer ingen adgang politik af sin egen, hvor pakken filter er den eneste grænse til rådighed."

# libretranslate
msgid "Bounds scope; bigger surface to ship cleanly first."
msgstr "Bounds omfang; større overflade til skibet rent først."

