# libretranslate
msgid "The [alias](https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/alias) repository is the RECOMMENDED way to define CLI shortcuts so frequently used commands do not have to be retyped. The effective repository is the `INFINITO_ALIAS_REPOSITORY` value in the generated `.env`."
msgstr "Den [alias](https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/alias) depot er den ANBEFALEDE måde at definere CLI genveje så ofte anvendte kommandoer ikke behøver at blive omskrevet. Det effektive lager er `INFINITO_ALIAS_REPOSITORY` værdi i genereret `.env`."

# libretranslate
msgid "The [lint.md](testing/lint.md) page covers repository-wide code quality expectations such as diff quality, maintainability, and conventions."
msgstr "Den [lint.md](testing/lint.md) side dækker datalagrings- bred kode kvalitet forventninger såsom diff- kvalitet, holdbarhed, og konventioner."

# libretranslate
msgid "The [per-role meta layout](../contributing/design/role/services/layout.md) already lists `addons`, `plugins`, and `modules` among the keys *inlined* under the primary service entity. This requirement promotes that concept to a first-class, per-file `meta/addons/<addon_id>.yml` topic (one file per addon, file root IS the addon spec), the same move requirement 011 made for `meta/info.yml` and requirement 008/009 made for other meta topics."
msgstr "Den [per- rolle meta layout](../contributing/design/role/services/layout.md) allerede lister `addons`, `plugins`, og `modules` blandt nøglerne *inlinet* under den primære tjenesteenhed. Dette krav fremmer dette koncept til en første klasse, per- fil `meta/addons/<addon_id>.yml` emne (én fil per addon, filroot IS addon spec), det samme bevægelseskrav 011 fremstillet til `meta/info.yml` og krav 008/009 lavet til andre meta emner."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `.onion` is a **deploy-time input**: a CLI helper mints the v3 key offline during inventory build, vaults it, and sets `DOMAIN_PRIMARY`. It must NOT be a runtime fact — `DOMAIN_PRIMARY` is consumed at build time (LDAP base, CA, applications cache). The role restores the minted key into the hidden-service volume before Tor starts."
msgstr "Den `.onion` er **deploy- time input**: en CLI hjælper mints v3 nøgle offline under lageropbygning, hvælver det, og sæt `DOMAIN_PRIMARY`. Det må ikke være en runtime fact - `DOMAIN_PRIMARY` forbruges på byggetid (LDAP base, CA, applikationer cache). Rollen genopretter tasten i hidden- service volumen før Tor starter."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `@playwright/test` version pinned into the rendered `package.json` comes from `playwright.version` in `roles/test-e2e-playwright/meta/services.yml` via the `image_version` filter. That YAML value is the single source of truth for the Playwright version."
msgstr "Den `@playwright/test` version fastgjort i den afleverede `package.json` kommer fra `playwright.version` til `roles/test-e2e-playwright/meta/services.yml` via `image_version` filter. Den YAML værdi er den eneste kilde til sandhed for Playwright version."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `API.cloudflare.api_token` value (declared in `group_vars/all/18_api.yml`, read via `lookup('api', 'cloudflare.api_token')`) must contain a valid Cloudflare API Token.   This token is used for all DNS operations and ACME (SSL/TLS certificate) challenges that require access to your Cloudflare-managed domains."
msgstr "Den `API.cloudflare.api_token` værdi (angivet i `group_vars/all/18_api.yml`, læse via `lookup('api', 'cloudflare.api_token')`) skal indeholde et gyldigt Cloudflare API Token. Denne token bruges til alle DNS-operationer og ACME (SSL / TLS-certifikat) udfordringer, der kræver adgang til dine cloudflare-styrede domæner."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `Bash(*)` allow grants broad access to the `docker` CLI (alongside every other shell command) under the assumption that no production containers share the host. Non-mutating-image subcommands (`rm`, `kill`, `stop`, `system prune`, `volume rm`, `cp`) can disrupt or destroy container state. Under test-only usage, the blast radius is bounded to ephemeral state that can be recreated from the compose stack."
msgstr "Den `Bash(*)` at give tilskud bred adgang til `docker` CLI (ved siden af enhver anden skalkommando) under forudsætning af, at ingen produktionsbeholdere deler værten. Ikke- mutations- billed- underkommandoer (`rm`, `kill`, `stop`, `system prune`, `volume rm`, `cp`) kan forstyrre eller ødelægge container tilstand. Under test- kun brug, sprængradius er afgrænset til efemeral tilstand, der kan gendannes fra komponen stak."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `Bash(*)` allow lets the agent run any Makefile target without prompting. The `Makefile` is checked into git and reviewed on every pull request, so targets themselves are trusted. Every action a target performs still runs inside the sandbox."
msgstr "Den `Bash(*)` tillade agent køre enhver Makefile mål uden at spørge. Den `Makefile` er tjekket ind i git og revideret på hver pull anmodning, så mål selv er betroet. Alle handlinger, et mål udfører, kører stadig i sandkassen."

# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The `Corefile.tmpl` MUST be the source of truth. It is rendered to `Corefile` by [coredns.py](../../cli/administration/deploy/development/coredns.py), which substitutes its `${VAR}` placeholders in-process, using values from `.env` (generated from [default.env](../../default.env), overridable through the CLI's environment)."
msgstr "Den `Corefile.tmpl` Det må være sandhedens kilde. Det er givet til `Corefile` af [coredns.py](../../cli/administration/deploy/development/coredns.py), der erstatter `${VAR}` pladsholdere i-proces, ved hjælp af værdier fra `.env` (genereret fra [default.env](../../default.env), kan overrides gennem CLI miljø)."

