# libretranslate
msgid "The audit MUST classify these as `db-extension` (out of scope), so a later sweep does not mistake them for app addons. If a future role mixes app addons and DB extensions under one key, the migration MUST split them by destination."
msgstr "Revisionen skal klassificere disse som `db-extension` (uden for anvendelsesområdet), så en senere sweep ikke forveksler dem for app addons. Hvis en fremtidig rolle blander app addons og DB udvidelser under en nøgle, skal migreringen opdele dem efter destination."

# libretranslate
msgid "The audit is the role tree itself: every fact about a role's MCP surface lives in its own `meta/services.yml`, so a separate artifact would be a copy that can go stale. `grep -l '^mcp:' roles/*/meta/services.yml` enumerates the integrated roles."
msgstr "Revisionen er selve rolletræet: Enhver kendsgerning om en rolles MCP overflade lever i sin egen `meta/services.yml`, Så en separat artefakt ville være en kopi, der kan blive gammel. `grep -l '^mcp:' roles/*/meta/services.yml` opregner de integrerede roller."

# libretranslate
msgid "The automatic pin follows the effective deploy mode, and in swarm it must NOT be ``host-gateway``: that alias resolves per node, while openresty publishes :80 with ``mode: host`` under ``node.role == manager``, so every replica on a worker dialled its own gateway and the token exchange died with 'Connection refused' (7b1839681, measured on penpot in run 31340965955). Swarm therefore gets the stack host's routable address -- the destination svc-net-tor already sends all hidden-service traffic to. ``ansible_facts`` carries it because the compose file is rendered once with the manager as inventory host and swarm applies the same ``extra_hosts`` to every task."
msgstr "Den automatiske pin følger den effektive deployeringstilstand, og i sværm må den IKKE være ``host-gateway``: at alias løser per node, mens openresty offentliggør:80 med ``mode: host`` under ``node.role == manager``, så hver kopi på en arbejder ringede sin egen gateway og token udveksling døde med 'Connection afvist' (7b1839681, målt på pench in run 31340965955). Varm derfor får stack værtens routable adresse -- destinationen svc-net-tor allerede sender alle skjulte-service trafik til. ``ansible_facts`` bærer det, fordi komponér filen er afleveret én gang med lederen som lagervært og sværm anvender den samme ``extra_hosts`` til alle opgaver."

# libretranslate
msgid "The axis suffix a CI selection token may carry (``#0,2@swarm+tor``) is split off before the lookup and re-attached after it, so translating a list never drops what the operator pinned on it."
msgstr "Axis suffiks en CI markering token kan bære (``#0,2@swarm+tor``) er opdelt før opslag og omhæftning efter det, så oversætte en liste aldrig falder, hvad operatøren fastgjort på det."

# libretranslate
msgid "The backup host is NOT appended to the cluster inventory: it lives in a sibling ``backup.yml`` next to ``INV_PATH`` (same host_vars dir), deployed as a second play after the cluster one. Without a svc-swarm-node group that play resolves DEPLOYMENT_MODE=compose and IS_STACK_HOST=true on the backup host, so the backup roles run without cluster-membership special cases."
msgstr "Backup værten er IKKE knyttet til klyngeoversigten: den lever i en søskende ``backup.yml`` ud for ``INV_PATH`` (samme host_vars dir), indsat som et andet stykke efter klyngen en. Uden svc-swarm-node gruppe, der spiller løser DEPLOYMENT_MODE= sammensætning og IS_STACK_HOST= true på backup vært, så backup roller køre uden cluster- medlemskab særlige tilfælde."

# libretranslate
msgid "The base URL of the running server."
msgstr "BasisURL 'en for den kørende server."

# libretranslate
msgid "The behaviour is fail-loud by design. Missing or mistyped secret names MUST surface as a failed workflow run rather than as a PR with an unintended author."
msgstr "Den adfærd er fejl- højt af design. Manglende eller misbrugte hemmelige navne SKAL overflade som en mislykket workflow køre snarere end som en PR med en utilsigtet forfatter."

# libretranslate
msgid "The branch MUST exist and MUST NOT be checked out anywhere else; resolve a collision with `make worktree-prune` or `make worktree-down` first. Pass `base=<dir>` only when the operator names a different parent directory, and then repeat that same `base=` in every later `make worktree-down` call."
msgstr "Filialen SKAL eksistere og må ikke kontrolleres andre steder; løse en kollision med `make worktree-prune` eller `make worktree-down` Først. Pass `base=<dir>` kun når operatøren nævner en anden forældremappe, og derefter gentage det samme `base=` hver anden uge `make worktree-down` Ring."

# libretranslate
msgid "The branch prefix MUST match the detected scope, otherwise the `validate-pr-branch-prefix` job fails."
msgstr "Filialpræfikset SKAL matche det fundne anvendelsesområde, ellers skal `validate-pr-branch-prefix` job mislykkes."

# libretranslate
msgid "The branch prefix MUST match the type of change. The [PR workflow](pull-request.md) uses it to classify the scope and decide which CI pipeline to run."
msgstr "Filialpræfikset SKAL svare til typen af ændring. Den [PR workflow](pull-request.md) bruger det til at klassificere anvendelsesområdet og beslutte, hvilken CI-rørledning der skal køre."

# libretranslate
msgid "The branch-name matcher normally also requires the run's head repository to be the pull request's own. Two cases relax that: a run whose `head_repository` the API omits, and a pull request whose head fork has been deleted, where the event payload carries no head repository either. Both are matched on the branch name alone, because otherwise their runs would keep going forever — and neither field is something a contributor can influence. The ambiguity check above is what makes that safe: it runs whenever a head branch is known, with or without a repository, so a shared branch name still disables the matcher rather than cancelling the wrong pull request."
msgstr "Den branchenavn matcher normalt også kræver løbets hoved arkiv at være pull anmodning egen. To tilfælde slappe af, at: en køre, hvis `head_repository` i API udelader, og en pull anmodning, hvis hoved gaffel er blevet slettet, hvor begivenheden nyttelast bærer heller ikke hoved lager. Begge er matchet på filialnavnet alene, fordi ellers ville deres løb fortsætte for evigt - og ingen af felterne er noget, en bidragyder kan påvirke. Uklarhedstjekket ovenfor er, hvad der gør dette sikkert: Det kører, når en hovedgren er kendt, med eller uden et lager, så et delt grennavn stadig deaktiverer matcheren i stedet for at annullere den forkerte pull anmodning."

# libretranslate
msgid "The bridge activates only when `PROXY_HEADER_SSO` is truthy (derived from `lookup('sso', application_id, 'is_proxy_gated')`); otherwise the middleware is a transparent pass-through and the native password form still guards `/admin`."
msgstr "Broen aktiveres kun når `PROXY_HEADER_SSO` er sandy (afledt af `lookup('sso', application_id, 'is_proxy_gated')`); ellers midterware er en gennemsigtig pass- through og den indfødte password form stadig vagter `/admin`."

# libretranslate
msgid "The bridge activates only when ``PROXY_HEADER_SSO`` is truthy (derived from ``lookup('sso', application_id, 'is_proxy_gated')``); otherwise the middleware is a transparent pass-through and the native password form still guards ``/admin``."
