msgid "The full CSP test surface lives in the same module: `assertCspResponseHeader(response, label)` (returns the parsed directive map), `assertCspMetaParity(page, headerDirectives, label)` (verifies the optional `<meta http-equiv>` echo is a subset of the response header), `installCspViolationObserver(page)` + `readCspViolations(page)` (DOM-side `securitypolicyviolation` capture), `expectNoCspViolations(page, diagnostics, label)` (asserts neither the DOM stream nor `diagnostics.cspRelated` carries a violation), and the `EXPECTED_CSP_DIRECTIVES` constant. Specs MUST require these from `./personas`; inline copies are forbidden and caught at review."
msgstr "Den fulde CSP-testoverflade lever i samme modul: `assertCspResponseHeader(response, label)` (returnerer det fortolkede direktivkort), `assertCspMetaParity(page, headerDirectives, label)` (kontrollerer valgmuligheden `<meta http-equiv>` echo er en delmængde af responsheader), `installCspViolationObserver(page)` + `readCspViolations(page)` (DOM- side `securitypolicyviolation` indfangning), `expectNoCspViolations(page, diagnostics, label)` (hævder hverken DOM stream eller `diagnostics.cspRelated` bærer en overtrædelse), og `EXPECTED_CSP_DIRECTIVES` konstant. Specifikationer skal kræve disse fra `./personas`; inline kopier er forbudt og fanget ved revision."

