msgstr "Hovedformålet med denne rolle er at holde Docker miljøer rene ved at identificere og rapportere forældreløse anonyme mængder. Det understøtter en whitelist mekanisme til at undgå advarsel om kendte eller forsætlige mængder."

# libretranslate
msgid "The main purpose of this role is to:"
msgstr "Hovedformålet med denne rolle er at:"

# libretranslate
msgid "The maintained native path needs Kibana Agent Builder with its index privileges and licence; the older sidecar is deprecated."
msgstr "Den vedligeholdte indfødte sti har brug for Kibana Agent Builder med sine indeksrettigheder og certifikat; den ældre sidevogn er forældet."

# libretranslate
msgid "The maintained native path requires Kibana Agent Builder, suitable index/application privileges, and licensing; the older sidecar is deprecated. Record `missing_kibana_and_licence` until those dependencies are explicit."
msgstr "Den vedligeholdte indfødte sti kræver Kibana Agent Builder, passende indeks / ansøgning privilegier, og licens; den ældre sidevogn er forældet. Optag `missing_kibana_and_licence` indtil disse afhængigheder er eksplicitte."

# libretranslate
msgid "The make target ultimately calls the same CLI, so any behaviour described here applies to both."
msgstr "Målet kalder i sidste ende den samme CLI, så enhver adfærd beskrevet her gælder for begge."

# libretranslate
msgid "The manager legs of steps 2, 4 and 9 run only when the app's include closure contains `svc-bkp-volume-2-local` / `svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`. `utils/tests/swarm/backup_repos.py` derives both the manager's inventory groups and the `remote-2-local` provider list from that closure; apps without those roles prove the chain through the nfs repository."
msgstr "Styreben af trin 2, 4 og 9 køre kun når appens indeholder lukning `svc-bkp-volume-2-local` / `svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`. `utils/tests/swarm/backup_repos.py` udleder både bestyrerens beholdningsgrupper og `remote-2-local` udbyder liste fra denne lukning; apps uden disse roller bevise kæden gennem nfs repository."

# libretranslate
msgid "The manifest document, or None when the generation carries none."
msgstr "Det manifest dokument, eller ingen, når generation bærer ingen."

# libretranslate
msgid "The manual entry workflow (`entry-manual-steer.yml`) sets `cancel-in-progress: true` on its own group, and the orchestrator's group cancels for `workflow_dispatch` regardless of ref, so a manual sweep supersedes on both levels, `main` included."
msgstr "Arbejdsgangen ved manuel indgang (`entry-manual-steer.yml`) sæt `cancel-in-progress: true` på sin egen gruppe, og orkesterens gruppe annullerer for `workflow_dispatch` Uanset ref, så en manuel feje erstatter på begge niveauer, `main` inkluderet."

# libretranslate
msgid "The marked row carries `instructions: <mode>` in the matrix JSON and a 📖 in its job title, between the variant number and the ⭐ of a priority row."
msgstr "Den markerede række bærer `instructions: <mode>` i matrix JSON og en 📖 i sin stillingsbetegnelse, mellem variantnummeret og den prioriterede række."

# libretranslate
msgid "The marker file carries the same name as the swarm drill's (`scripts/tests/deploy/swarm/routine/backup/base.sh`) — one name for one concept. The implementations stay apart on purpose: the swarm drill follows a single token across five hops on four machines from the controller, which has nothing in common with marking every subject of one host beyond the three lines that write a file and read it back."
msgstr "Markørfilen bærer samme navn som sværmboret. (`scripts/tests/deploy/swarm/routine/backup/base.sh`) - et navn for et koncept. Implementeringerne holdes adskilt med vilje: sværmboret følger en enkelt token på tværs af fem humle på fire maskiner fra controlleren, som ikke har noget til fælles med at markere hvert emne af en vært ud over de tre linjer, der skriver en fil og læse den tilbage."

# libretranslate
msgid "The match stream is built once per process by `_scan.iter_matches` and shared across the four test classes; the repo-derived context (application defaults, user defaults, per-role schemas, `application_id`-declaring role set) comes from `_scan.get_context`. Validation helpers live in `_validate.py`. Suppression is wired through the project's `noqa` / `nocheck` grammar; the rule key is `lookup-config-path` (see [suppression.md](../../../../../docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md))."
msgstr "Matchstrømmen er bygget en gang pr. proces ved `_scan.iter_matches` og delt på tværs af de fire testklasser; den repoafledte kontekst (applikationsstandard, brugerstandard, perrolleskema `application_id`-erklære rolle sæt) kommer fra `_scan.get_context`. Validering hjælpere lever i `_validate.py`. Undertrykkelse er forbundet gennem projektets `noqa` / `nocheck` grammatik; regelnøglen er `lookup-config-path` (Se [suppression.md](../../../../../docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md))."

# libretranslate
msgid "The matcher itself lives in :mod:`utils.cache.gitignore` (single SPOT for ``.gitignore`` parsing and matching). :func:`iter_non_ignored_files` here composes the cached project walk with that matcher and is the recommended helper for lint tests that want the \"files git would track\" view without subprocessing."
msgstr "Selve matcheren bor i :mod:`utils.cache.gitignore` (enkelt SPOT for ``.gitignore`` parsing og matching). :func:`iter_non_ignored_files` her komponerer caching projekt gå med at matcher og er den anbefalede hjælper til flint test, der ønsker \"filer git ville spore\" visning uden underbehandling."

# libretranslate
msgid "The matching Pull Request template defines PR structure, required author input, and review context. You MUST use the guidance in [Pull Request Templates](../artefact/git/pull-request.md) and orient your Pull Request to it."
msgstr "Den matchende Pull Request skabelon definerer PR struktur, krævede forfatter input, og gennemse sammenhæng. Du skal bruge vejledningen i [Træk anmodningsskabeloner](../artefact/git/pull-request.md) og orientere din Pull Request til det."

# libretranslate
msgid "The materialised application payload exposes services under the bare ``services`` key (no ``compose.services`` wrapper). The function name is preserved for backwards compatibility with existing call sites."
msgstr "Den materialiserede anvendelse nyttelast udsætter tjenester under bare ``services`` nøgle (ng ``compose.services`` papir). Funktionsnavnet bevares for baglæns kompatibilitet med eksisterende opkaldssteder."

# libretranslate
msgid "The matrix hands every row exactly one filesystem, so the value a deploy job sees is always narrow. Reading that narrowness as a demand would turn every condition the applying step is built to tolerate into a red row: a loop device it could not claim, a pool another job still holds, a kernel without the module."
msgstr "Den matrix hænder hver række præcis én filsystem, så værdien en implementering job ser er altid smal. At læse, at smalhed som et krav ville vende enhver betingelse det anvendte trin er bygget til at tolerere i en rød række: en løkke enhed, det ikke kunne hævde, en pool et andet job stadig holder, en kerne uden modulet."

msgid "The matrix is **directional** (the row hosts the plugin/flag); bidirectional pairs such as `nextcloud`↔`openproject` carry a symbol in both cells. It is generated by [cli/build/docs/integration_matrix](../../cli/build/docs/integration_matrix/__main__.py): ☑️ edges are scanned from every role's `meta/services.yml` (the `sso`/`matomo`/`prometheus`/`email`/`dashboard`/`css`/`logout`/`cdn`/`coturn`/`collabora`/`onlyoffice`/`libretranslate` keys), and ✅/🪙 edges come from a curated, web-verified `EDGES` map. It MUST be regenerated rather than hand-edited. At creation time it covers 82 roles with **523 infinito-native (☑️) wired edges plus 96 curated upstream (✅/🪙) edges**. The ☑️ layer is exhaustive (it is scanned from the repo); the ✅/🪙 layer is **not yet exhaustive** and grows as each role's upstream plugin ecosystem is researched in depth (e.g. a MediaWiki deep-dive added `DiscourseSsoConsumer`, `PeerTubeEmbed`, `MachineTranslation`→libretranslate, `Extension:AWS`→minio, and an LLM editor→openwebui). The ✅/🪙 set is the **backlog**: every ✅ pair is an addon this requirement commits to declare and wire (see Acceptance Criteria), and completing the per-role upstream survey is itself an acceptance criterion."
msgstr ""

msgid "The matrix is **directional**: the row hosts the plugin/flag. Bidirectional pairs (e.g. `nextcloud`↔`openproject`) carry a symbol in both cells, each linking to that side."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "The matrix orchestrator (`utils/tests/swarm/matrix.py`) drives the deploy stage per variant round; `routine/00_one.sh` drives the surrounding stages for one distro, and the workflow `.github/workflows/call-test-deploy.yml` drives the distro loop. Run one app locally with `make swarm-zombie app=<id>` (keeps the cluster for inspection) or the whole matrix via `make roundtrip`."
msgstr "Matrixorkestratoren (`utils/tests/swarm/matrix.py`) driver implementeringsfasen pr. variant-runde `routine/00_one.sh` Kører de omgivende stadier for én ditro, og arbejdsgangen `.github/workflows/call-test-deploy.yml` Kører Distro Loop. Kør en app lokalt med `make swarm-zombie app=<id>` (holder klyngen til inspektion) eller hele matrixen via `make roundtrip`."

# libretranslate
msgid "The matrix orchestrator needs these before it provisions, so that the authorized_keys reach host_vars through the merging ``--vars`` channel rather than through the replacing extra-vars file."
msgstr "Den matrix orkestrator har brug for disse, før det leverer, så authorized_keys rækkevidde host_vars gennem fusioneringen ``--vars`` kanal snarere end gennem den erstatter ekstravars fil."

# libretranslate
msgid "The matrix-variant planner (see [variants.md](variants.md)) calls the expansion once per round, so each round's inventory gets the right transitive closure for that round's variant set."
msgstr "Matrix- variantplanlæggeren (Se [variants.md](variants.md)) kalder udvidelse en gang per runde, så hver rundes opgørelse får den rigtige transitive lukning for den rundes variant sæt."

# libretranslate
msgid "The mautrix network bridges are declared in [`meta/addons/`](./meta/addons/) as `mechanism: bridge` addons (requirement 026, Decision 13). Each is `required: false` and **disabled by default**; its per-network DB password and its appservice `as_token`/`hs_token` pair are referenced from [`meta/secrets.yml`](./meta/secrets.yml) `credentials:`, never inlined. The role renders each bridge's `config.yaml` and the matching Synapse `registration.yaml` from the same tokens."
msgstr "De mautrix netværk broer er erklæret i [`meta/addons/`](./meta/addons/) som `mechanism: bridge` addons (krav 026, afgørelse 13)Hver er `required: false` og **deaktiveret som standard**; dens password for menunetværk DB og dens appservice `as_token`/`hs_token` par er refereret fra [`meta/secrets.yml`](./meta/secrets.yml) `credentials:`, aldrig antydet. Rollen gør hver bro 's `config.yaml` og den matchende Synapse `registration.yaml` fra de samme tokens."

# libretranslate
msgid "The mautrix network bridges are declared in ```meta/addons/`` <./meta/addons/>`__ as ``mechanism: bridge`` addons (requirement 026, Decision 13). Each is ``required: false`` and **disabled by default**; its per-network DB password and its appservice ``as_token``/``hs_token`` pair are referenced from ```meta/secrets.yml`` <./meta/secrets.yml>`__ ``credentials:``, never inlined. The role renders each bridge’s ``config.yaml`` and the matching Synapse ``registration.yaml`` from the same tokens."
msgstr "De mautrix netværk broer er erklæret i ```meta/addons/`` <./meta/addons/>`__ as ``mechanism: bridge`` addons (requirement 026, Decision 13). Each is ``required: false`` and **disabled by default**; its per-network DB password and its appservice ``as_token``/``hs_token`` pair are referenced from ```meta/secrets.yml`` <./meta/secrets.yml>`__ ``credentials:``, never inlined. The role renders each bridge’s ``config.yaml`` and the matching Synapse ``registration.yaml`` fra de samme tokens."

msgid "The merged map is what the inventory ALSO bakes into host_vars, so feeding the same dict into `CombinedResolver(services_overrides=...)` eliminates the topology-vs-host_vars drift that variant-blind resolution produced."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "The metrics endpoint needs a server-generated token that cannot be pre-seeded into a static scrape config from the inventory. Same pattern as `web-app-gitea`. Gives the `openbao_core_unsealed` gauge."
msgstr "Den metrics endpoint har brug for en servergenereret token, der ikke kan forudsedes i en statisk skrabe config fra opgørelsen. Samme mønster som `web-app-gitea`. Giver den `openbao_core_unsealed` mål."

# libretranslate
msgid "The minimum env set for any spec following the persona flows is `APP_BASE_URL`, `CANONICAL_DOMAIN`, and `LOGOUT_URL`. `DASHBOARD_BASE_URL` is rendered only by the dashboard role's own spec, because consumer personas enter at `APP_BASE_URL` directly. Specs that gate on auth additionally read at least one of `OIDC_ISSUER_URL`, `KEYCLOAK_BASE_URL`, plus the persona credentials `ADMIN_USERNAME` / `ADMIN_PASSWORD` and `BIBER_USERNAME` / `BIBER_PASSWORD`. Specs that exercise integrations (Matomo, Discourse, Email, Prometheus, …) read the integration-specific keys defined in [Agent `playwright.env.j2`](../../../../agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md)."
msgstr "Den mindste env sæt for enhver spec efter persona strømme er `APP_BASE_URL`, `CANONICAL_DOMAIN`, og `LOGOUT_URL`. `DASHBOARD_BASE_URL` er kun gjort af instrumentbrættets rolle egen spec, fordi forbrugerne personas ind på `APP_BASE_URL` direkte. Spekter, der gate på auth desuden læse mindst en af `OIDC_ISSUER_URL`, `KEYCLOAK_BASE_URL`, plus persona akkreditiver `ADMIN_USERNAME` / `ADMIN_PASSWORD` og `BIBER_USERNAME` / `BIBER_PASSWORD`. Spekter, der udøver integration (Matomo, Discourse, e-mail, Prometheus,...) læse de integrations-specifikke nøgler defineret i [Agent `playwright.env.j2`](../../../../agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md)."

# libretranslate
msgid "The mirror workflow runs as stage 8 of the CI pipeline. See [ci.md](../git/pipeline.md). It runs in parallel with the DNS tests and MUST complete before deploy tests start."
msgstr "Spejlet workflow kører som scenen 8 af CI-rørledningen. Se [ci.md](../git/pipeline.md). Det kører parallelt med DNS-test og SKAL fuldføre før implementering test starter."

# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The mirrors file is generated into the inventory directory. The inventory creator applies mirror image overrides to host variables via `cli/administration/inventory/provision/mirror_overrides.py`, which reads `mirrors.yml.applications` and writes `applications.{role}.services.{service}.image` (and `.version`) into host vars subject to the per-service `mirror_policy`."
msgstr "Spejlfilen genereres i lagermappen. Opgørelsesskaberen anvender spejlbillede tilsidesætter til vært variabler via `cli/administration/inventory/provision/mirror_overrides.py`, der lyder: `mirrors.yml.applications` og skriver `applications.{role}.services.{service}.image` (og `.version`) i værtsvogne, der er omfattet af per- service `mirror_policy`."

# libretranslate
msgid "The mode is read as ``compose_mode_force or DEPLOYMENT_MODE`` rather than the bare cluster mode, because ``container_networks`` resolves attachments through that same effective mode: a role with an override must not lose its pin and its overlay at once."
msgstr "Tilstanden læses som ``compose_mode_force or DEPLOYMENT_MODE`` snarere end bare klyngetilstand, fordi ``container_networks`` løser vedhæftede filer gennem den samme effektive tilstand: En rolle med en override må ikke miste sin nål og dens overlay på én gang."

# libretranslate
msgid "The mode selection is a *filter*, not an axis: ``--modes swarm`` keeps the rows whose role can be deployed as a swarm stack, ``--modes \"compose swarm\"`` keeps the rows at least one of the two can take. The shared filter is mode-clause + INFINITO_WHITELIST + INFINITO_BLACKLIST, the order is INFINITO_DISCOVERY_SORT, whose first key sorts clones last (one representative per dna cluster stays ahead of the budget cut, so redundant same-service-set variants fall behind it first), and the lifecycle envelope is INFINITO_LIFECYCLES."
msgstr "Tilstandsvalget er en *filter*, ikke en akse: ``--modes swarm`` holder rækker, hvis rolle kan indsættes som en sværm stak, ``--modes \"compose swarm\"`` holder rækkerne mindst en af de to kan tage. Det delte filter er mode- klausul + INFINITO_WHITELIST + INFINITO_BLACKLIST, ordren er INFINITO_DISCOVERY_SORT, hvis første nøgle slags kloner sidste (en repræsentant per DNA klynge forbliver foran budgetnedskæringer, så overflødige same-service-sæt varianter falder bag det først), og livscykluskonvolutten er INFINITO_LIFECYCLES."

# libretranslate
msgid "The mode sequence defaults to `compose swarm` and is overridable with `modes=\"compose swarm\"`. The order is always compose first, so the cheaper mode fails fast before the expensive swarm rebuild. Append `k8s` here once that mode exists."
msgstr "Modesekvensen er standard til `compose swarm` og kan overgås med `modes=\"compose swarm\"`. Ordren er altid komponere først, så den billigere tilstand mislykkes hurtigt før den dyre sværm genopbygge. Tilføj `k8s` Her, når den tilstand eksisterer."

# libretranslate
msgid "The mode the guide would replay *app* in, or ``''`` when it cannot."
msgstr "Den tilstand guiden ville genspille *app* i, eller ``''`` når det ikke kan."

# libretranslate
msgid "The module is deliberately free of deploy-runtime imports: the CI selection resolves its closure on a runner that has no inventory, no container and no `INFINITO_SRC_DIR`."
msgstr "Modulet er bevidst frit for deploy- runtime import: CI udvælgelse løser sin lukning på en runner, der ikke har nogen opgørelse, ingen container og ingen `INFINITO_SRC_DIR`."

# libretranslate
msgid "The mount MUST be available before Docker starts. Otherwise the daemon may fall back to the system drive or fail to start cleanly."
msgstr "Monteret SKAL være tilgængeligt før Docker starter. Ellers dæmonen kan falde tilbage til systemet drev eller undlader at starte rent."

# libretranslate
msgid "The name never holds a space: the ``whitelist`` and ``priority`` workflow inputs are space-separated lists, so a display name with a space in it would make a two-role list unparseable."
msgstr "Navnet har aldrig et mellemrum: ``whitelist`` og ``priority`` workflow indgange er mellemrum-adskilt lister, så et display navn med et rum i det ville gøre en torolleliste unparseable."

# libretranslate
msgid "The name of the matching role directory."
msgstr "Navnet på den matchende rollemappe."

# libretranslate
msgid "The names in declaration order, aliases substituted."
msgstr "Navnene i deklarationsrækkefølge, aliasser erstattet."

# libretranslate
msgid "The names payload is stored under in THIS generation."
msgstr "Navnene nyttelast er gemt under i denne generation."

msgid "The naming conventions below are additionally checked locally by the lint test [test_branch_name.py](../../../../tests/lint/repository/naming/test_branch_name.py), which fails `make test-lint` when the checked-out branch uses an unknown prefix (e.g. `feat/` instead of `feature/`) or a non-kebab-case description."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "The narrow case is what a deploy job actually sees, because the matrix hands every row exactly one kind. Reading that narrowness as a demand would turn every condition the applying step tolerates into a red row on every deploy: a loop device it could not claim, a pool another job still holds. The run's own input decides instead."
msgstr "Den smalle sag er, hvad en implementering job faktisk ser, fordi matrixen hænder hver række præcis én slags. At læse, at smalle som et krav ville gøre hver betingelse det anvendte trin tolererer i en rød række på hver implementering: en løkke enhed, det ikke kunne hævde, en pool en anden job stadig holder. Løbets eget input bestemmer i stedet."

# libretranslate
msgid "The next `make compose-deploy mode=update apps=web-app-hugo` will pull the image, restart nginx, and serve the freshly rendered output."
msgstr "Den næste `make compose-deploy mode=update apps=web-app-hugo` vil trække billedet, genstarte nginx, og tjene frisk leveret output."

# libretranslate
msgid "The next stage in the pipeline MUST NOT execute when the previous stage classified the plugin as `incompatible`."
msgstr "Det næste trin i rørledningen SKAL IKKE udføres, når den foregående fase klassificeret plugin som `incompatible`."

# libretranslate
msgid "The nfs-server uses the userspace `nfs-ganesha` (`ganesha`) flavor in every runtime; `services.nfs-server.flavor` in `roles/svc-storage-nfs-server/meta/services.yml` is the SPOT, and `kernel` is a per-inventory override. Ganesha is packaged for the `Debian` and `RedHat` os families only. Kernel `nfsd` in a privileged DinD node is wedge-prone: the export can be present yet the controller mount returns ENOENT, and `exportfs` can stick in D-state. If a swarm step hangs at `Reload NFS exports` from a stuck kernel-NFS mount, you MUST recover with `make swarm-clean` on the host; see the NFS gotcha in [Roundtrip Loop](roundtrip.md). You MUST NOT fall back to a compose-only sweep while swarm is blocked."
msgstr "Nfs- serveren bruger brugerrummet `nfs-ganesha` (`ganesha`) smag i hver runtime; `services.nfs-server.flavor` til `roles/svc-storage-nfs-server/meta/services.yml` er SPOT, og `kernel` er en per- opgørelse override. Ganesha er pakket til `Debian` og `RedHat` Kun os familier. Kernel `nfsd` i en privilegeret DinD node er kile- prone: eksporten kan være til stede, men controller mount returnerer ENOENT, og `exportfs` kan holde sig i D-tilstand. Hvis et sværmskridt hænger ved `Reload NFS exports` fra en fast kernel- NFS mount, skal du komme sig med `make swarm-clean` på værten; se NFS fik cha i [Roundtrip Loop](roundtrip.md). Du må ikke falde tilbage til en komponist-kun feje mens sværmen er blokeret."

# libretranslate
msgid "The nightly timers (volume 01:00, nfs 01:30, secrets 01:45, device 02:00, remote pull 00:30) run independently of every step above and never fire during a lab run."
msgstr "De natlige timere (volumen 01:00, nfs 01:30, hemmeligheder 01:45, enhed 02:00, fjerntræk 00:30) køre uafhængigt af hvert trin over og aldrig skyde under en lab køre."

# libretranslate
msgid "The node hidden service exposes Mailu's mail ports in addition to `80`, via extra `HiddenServicePort` entries: `HiddenServicePort 25`, `587`, `465`, `143`, `993` → Mailu's local front binds on `127.0.0.1`. Mailu is then reachable at `<node>.onion` for SMTP/submission/IMAP."
msgstr "Den skjulte knude-service afslører Mailu's mail havne ud over `80`, via ekstra `HiddenServicePort` angivelser: `HiddenServicePort 25`, `587`, `465`, `143`, `993` → Mailu's lokale front bindes på `127.0.0.1`. Mailu er derefter tilgængelig på `<node>.onion` til SMTP/submission/IMAP."

# libretranslate
msgid "The number of discarded translations; their entries stay unchanged."
msgstr "Antallet af kasserede oversættelser; deres indlæg forbliver uændret."

# libretranslate
msgid "The number of dumps replayed."
msgstr "Antallet af lossepladser genspillet."

# libretranslate
msgid "The oauth2 ACL in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml) blacklists only `/login`, and `sys-svc-proxy` renders a blacklist as *expose everything by default, then protect the listed paths*. The helper lands on `/`, which is public, so the proxy never intercepts it and the Keycloak round trip never starts."
msgstr "Den oauth2 ACL in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml) Kun sortlister `/login`, og `sys-svc-proxy` gør en sortliste som *udsætte alt som standard, derefter beskytte de anførte stier*Hjælpen lander på `/`, som er offentlig, så proxy aldrig opsnapper det og Keycloak rundtur starter aldrig."

# libretranslate
msgid "The oauth2 ACL in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ blacklists only ``/login``, and ``sys-svc-proxy`` renders a blacklist as *expose everything by default, then protect the listed paths*. The helper lands on ``/``, which is public, so the proxy never intercepts it and the Keycloak round trip never starts."
msgstr "Den oauth2 ACL in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ blacklists only ``/login``, and ``sys-svc-proxy`` renders a blacklist as *expose everything by default, then protect the listed paths*. The helper lands on ``/``, som er offentlig, så proxy aldrig opsnapper det og Keycloak rundtur starter aldrig."

# libretranslate
msgid "The offered modes are already narrowed by the run's ``--modes`` input, the onion states by its ``--tor`` input and the two pools by ``--distros`` and ``--filesystem``, so this catches a pin that fights the role, the variant, or the run's own axes with one check each."
msgstr "De tilbudte tilstande er allerede indsnævret af løbets ``--modes`` input, løg stater ved sin ``--tor`` input og de to puljer ved ``--distros`` og ``--filesystem``, så dette fanger en nål, der bekæmper rollen, variant, eller løbets egne akser med en kontrol hver."

# libretranslate
msgid "The official Baserow SSO feature is Enterprise-only. This role instead gates the community image with the shared Keycloak oauth2-proxy and installs a small trusted-header bridge in the Baserow backend. The bridge trusts the identity headers injected by nginx after oauth2-proxy authentication and converts them into native Baserow JWT refresh/access tokens for the frontend."
msgstr "Tjenestemanden Baserow SSO-funktionen er kun Enterprise- kun. Denne rolle sætter i stedet det fælles image op med den fælles Keycloak oauth2-proxy og installerer en lille trusted- header bro i Baserow Bagenden. Broen stoler på de identitet headers injiceret af nginx efter oauth2-proxy autentificering og konverterer dem til indfødte Baserow JWT refresh / adgang tokens for frontend."

# libretranslate
msgid "The official installer is **downloaded at runtime** and verified before execution:"
msgstr "Den officielle installatør er **downloades ved runtime** og kontrolleret før udførelse:"

