msgstr "Sidecaren bliver aldrig sendt offentligt. En skinnefri sonde af ``/mcp`` på den offentlige vhost er besvaret med en SSO omdirigering, aldrig med en MCP svar."

# libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar is reachable on the container network only, so a client probes it from inside the stack:"
msgstr "Sidecaren kan kun nås på containernettet, så en klient sonder det indefra stakken:"

# libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar oauth2-proxy admits only the LibreTranslate administrator RBAC group and whitelists just the machine API paths (`/translate`, `/detect`, …); see [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml). Inside the app, authorisation is API-key-tier only and decoupled from the IdP, as documented under [Single sign-on](#single-sign-on) above. A non-admin visitor therefore has no UI session to drive, so [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) declares `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`. The `administrator` and `guest` personas run unconditionally."
msgstr "Sidecaren oauth2-proxy indrømmer kun LibreTranslate administrator RBAC gruppe og whitelists bare maskinen API stier (`/translate`, `/detect`,...); se [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml). Inde i appen, tilladelse er API-key- tier kun og afkoblet fra IdP, som dokumenteret under [Enkelt signalpå-](#single-sign-on) over. En ikke-admin besøgende derfor har ingen UI session til at køre, så [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) erklærer `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`. `administrator` og `guest` personas køre betingelsesløst."

# libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar oauth2-proxy admits only the LibreTranslate administrator RBAC group and whitelists just the machine API paths (``/translate``, ``/detect``, …); see ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. Inside the app, authorisation is API-key-tier only and decoupled from the IdP, as documented under `Single sign-on <#single-sign-on>`__ above. A non-admin visitor therefore has no UI session to drive, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas run unconditionally."
msgstr "Sidecaren oauth2-proxy indrømmer kun LibreTranslate administrator RBAC gruppe og whitelists bare maskinen API stier (``/translate``, ``/detect``,...); se ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. Inside the app, authorisation is API-key-tier only and decoupled from the IdP, as documented under `Enkelt signalpå- <#single-sign-on>`__ above. A non-admin visitor therefore has no UI session to drive, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas køre betingelsesløst."

# libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar reads its upstream credential from an ``upstream.env`` file rather than from the compose environment, because the app password does not exist when the stack is first rendered. ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ writes that file after the mint and recreates the sidecar through ``svc-ai-mcp-adapter``\\ ’s ``rebuild.yml``: ``compose up`` resolves ``env_file`` while creating the container, which a restart would not."
msgstr "Sidecaren læser sin opstrømskredit fra en ``upstream.env`` fil snarere end fra den komponere miljø, fordi app-kodeordet ikke eksisterer, når stakken er første rendt. ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ writes that file after the mint and recreates the sidecar through ``svc-ai-mcp-adapter``\\ ’s ``rebuild.yml``: ``compose up`` resolves ``env_file`` samtidig skabe beholderen, som en genstart ikke ville."

# libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar reads its upstream credential from an `upstream.env` file rather than from the compose environment, because the app password does not exist when the stack is first rendered. [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) writes that file after the mint and recreates the sidecar through `svc-ai-mcp-adapter`'s `rebuild.yml`: `compose up` resolves `env_file` while creating the container, which a restart would not."
msgstr "Sidecaren læser sin opstrømskredit fra en `upstream.env` fil snarere end fra den komponere miljø, fordi app-kodeordet ikke eksisterer, når stakken er første rendt. [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) skriver denne fil efter mynten og genskaber sidevognen gennem `svc-ai-mcp-adapter`s `rebuild.yml`: `compose up` resolves `env_file` samtidig skabe beholderen, som en genstart ikke ville."

# libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar starts with `-r` (read-only) and a scope list covering user, repository, issue, pull request, search, file, branch, tag, commit and release."
msgstr "Sidecaren starter med `-r` (read- only) og en programliste, der dækker bruger, lager, udstedelse, udtræk anmodning, søgning, fil, gren, tag, begå og frigive."

# libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar starts with ``-r`` (read-only) and a scope list covering user, repository, issue, pull request, search, file, branch, tag, commit and release."
msgstr "Sidecaren starter med ``-r`` (read- only) og en programliste, der dækker bruger, lager, udstedelse, udtræk anmodning, søgning, fil, gren, tag, begå og frigive."

# libretranslate
msgid "The single `make compose-deploy` target resolves one or more bundles into the role groups declared under `all.children` and feeds them into the standard local deploy flow when `bundles=<csv>` is set. The resolver is [`utils.inventory.bundle_apps`](../../utils/inventory/bundle_apps.py); it deduplicates across bundles and preserves declaration order."
msgstr "Den enkelte `make compose-deploy` Målsætningen løser en eller flere bundter i de rollegrupper, der er angivet under `all.children` og fodrer dem ind i standard lokal deployering flow, når `bundles=<csv>` Er klar. Løsningen er [`utils.inventory.bundle_apps`](../../utils/inventory/bundle_apps.py); det fordobler på tværs af bundter og bevarer deklaration ordre."

# libretranslate
msgid "The single-database dumps, and the cluster dumps, which name their instance in the file name and go through ``baudolo-restore cluster``."
msgstr "Single-database dumps, og klyngen dumps, som navngiver deres tilfælde i filnavnet og gå igennem ``baudolo-restore cluster``."

# libretranslate
msgid "The single-token `gh * <verb>*` patterns above only match when the third token starts with the verb. Compound names like `item-create` or `mark-template` slip through because the third token is the full compound, not the bare verb. These rules close that gap for Projects v2 mutations namespace-wide."
msgstr "Den ene-token `gh * <verb>*` mønstre over kun matche, når den tredje token starter med verbet. Sammensatte navne som `item-create` eller `mark-template` glider igennem, fordi den tredje token er det fulde stof, ikke det bare verbum. Disse regler lukker denne kløft for projekter v2 mutationer namespace-wide."

# libretranslate
msgid "The size is the config blob plus every layer blob, i.e. what a pull moves over the wire. A multi-platform index is resolved to the ``os_name``/``architecture`` manifest first."
msgstr "Størrelsen er den config blob plus hvert lag blob, dvs. hvad et træk bevæger sig over tråden. Et multiplatformindeks er løst til ``os_name``/``architecture`` manifestere først."

# libretranslate
msgid "The skill writes `.claude/settings.json` / `.claude/settings.local.json`, which is the source of truth for the permission model itself: allow/ask/deny rules, sandbox scope, env vars, and hook commands that run on every tool event. Auto-allowing it creates a privilege-escalation path where the agent can grant itself arbitrary new `allow` entries, install hooks that run arbitrary shell, or widen `sandbox.filesystem.allowWrite` / shrink `denyRead`, all without ever prompting. Sandbox write-scope does not stop this because `.` is in `allowWrite`. A single wildcard entry (`update-config*`) covers every current and future invocation shape in one rule."
msgstr "De færdigheder skriver `.claude/settings.json` / `.claude/settings.local.json`, som er kilden til sandheden for tilladelsesmodellen selv: allow/ask/deny regler, sandkasse omfang, env vars, og krog kommandoer, der kører på hver værktøj begivenhed. Auto- tillader det skaber en eskalering sti, hvor agenten kan give sig selv vilkårlige nye `allow` poster, installere kroge, der kører vilkårlig shell, eller udvide `sandbox.filesystem.allowWrite` / skrumpe `denyRead`, alle uden nogensinde at tilskynde. Sandbox write- scope stopper ikke dette, fordi `.` er i `allowWrite`. En enkelt wildcard indgang (`update-config*`) dækker alle nuværende og fremtidige invasionsformer i én regel."

# libretranslate
msgid "The slug comes from :func:`axes.artifact_slug`, the same call the matrix entry carries into the workflow, so the name this looks for and the name CI uploads cannot drift apart."
msgstr "Kuglen kommer fra :func:`axes.artifact_slug`, det samme opkald matrix indgangen bærer ind i arbejdsgangen, så navnet dette søger efter, og navnet CI uploads kan ikke flyde fra hinanden."

# libretranslate
msgid "The software's identity: its repository, read from the group_vars SPOT, its author and address."
msgstr "Softwaren identitet: dens arkiv, læse fra group_vars SPOT, dets forfatter og adresse."

# libretranslate
msgid "The source code of this software is publicly available for transparency, learning, and private use."
msgstr "Kildekoden for denne software er offentligt tilgængelig for gennemsigtighed, læring og privat brug."

# libretranslate
msgid "The source run read a window of the ranking, starting where *carried* put it (:func:`carried_index`) and stopping at its budget. Only the green part of that window is newly settled, so the answer is the last row of the leading run of *successful* rows behind the window's start, as a selection token -- a token still names the same row after the ranking shifts, a row count does not."
msgstr "Kilden køre læse et vindue af rangering, startende hvor *båret* put it (:func:`carried_index`) og stoppe på sit budget. Kun den grønne del af dette vindue er nyligt afgjort, så svaret er den sidste række af den førende køre af *vellykket* rækker bag vinduets start, som en markering token -- et token stadig navngiver den samme række efter rangering skift, en række tæller ikke."

# libretranslate
msgid "The source run's ``priority`` input, whole."
msgstr "Kilden kører ``priority`` input, hele."

# libretranslate
msgid "The spec MUST be at `roles/<role>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`. The role-relative path is the SPOT constant `ROLE_FILE_PLAYWRIGHT_SPEC` in [mapping.py](../../../../../utils/roles/mapping.py); registered as optional on `ROLE_TYPE_APPLICATION`, disallowed elsewhere."
msgstr "Spektret skal være på `roles/<role>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`. Den role- relative sti er SPOT konstant `ROLE_FILE_PLAYWRIGHT_SPEC` til [mapping.py](../../../../../utils/roles/mapping.py); registreret som valgfrit den `ROLE_TYPE_APPLICATION`, ikke tilladt andre steder."

# libretranslate
msgid "The split means contributors do not need to extend the allowlist for every new shell command: `Bash(*)` already covers them, and sandbox confinement bounds the blast radius. The `deny` list catches the small set of operations whose blast radius is destructive even within the sandbox. For example, `rm -rf .` would still erase the working tree and `.git/` because `.` is writable under `allowWrite`, so the `rm -rf*` deny rule closes that gap."
msgstr "De opdelte midler bidragydere behøver ikke at udvide listen for hver ny skalkommando: `Bash(*)` De dækker dem allerede, og indespærring af sandkassen begrænser eksplosionsradius. Den `deny` liste fanger det lille sæt operationer, hvis sprængradius er destruktiv selv inden for sandkassen. For eksempel, `rm -rf .` ville stadig slette det arbejdende træ og `.git/` fordi `.` er skrivbar under `allowWrite`, så `rm -rf*` Fornægte reglen lukker denne kløft."

# libretranslate
msgid "The stack deploy modes the CI test-deploy matrix (get_role_skip) covers."
msgstr "Stack-deployeringsformerne CI-testmatrixen (get_role_skip) dække."

# libretranslate
msgid "The stack provides on-prem data storage, a local AI-adjacent service, centralized identity, and secure exposure through a reverse proxy. This bundle is a skeleton activation map."
msgstr "Stakken giver on- prem datalagring, en lokal AI- tilstødende service, centraliseret identitet, og sikker eksponering gennem en omvendt proxy. Dette bundt er et skelet aktiveringskort."

# libretranslate
msgid "The stage a role is invoked in (deepest matching category wins)."
msgstr "Den fase, en rolle er påberåbt i (dybeste matchende gevinster i kategori)."

# libretranslate
msgid "The staging dir exists and contains a non-empty `.env`."
msgstr "Den iscenesættende dir eksisterer og indeholder en ikke-tom `.env`."

# libretranslate
msgid "The standard OIDC `sub` claim is permitted as an alternative when the application explicitly requires a UUID-shaped identifier and stores its own mapping table. In that case the role MUST document the deviation in its README."
msgstr "Standard OIDC `sub` krav er tilladt som alternativ, når ansøgningen udtrykkeligt kræver en UUID-formet identifikator og gemmer sin egen kortlægning. I så fald SKAL rollen dokumentere afvigelsen i README."

# libretranslate
msgid "The steps, and the repos whose manifest could not be read. A repo that cannot state its layout is skipped rather than guessed at, but it must not take the others with it: recovering two repos of three beats recovering none because one manifest is corrupt."
msgstr "De skridt, og de repoer, hvis manifest ikke kunne læses. En repo, der ikke kan angive dens layout er sprunget over snarere end gættet på, men det må ikke tage de andre med det: inddrive to repos af tre beats inddrive ingen, fordi en manifestation er korrupt."

# libretranslate
msgid "The stored bearer still authenticates"
msgstr "Den lagrede bærer autentificerer stadig"

# libretranslate
msgid "The subset path fails the run when:"
msgstr "Delpunktsstien fejler løbet, når:"

# libretranslate
msgid "The subtree mirrors the host-side `apps/` structure verb by verb and scope by scope:"
msgstr "Undertræet afspejler værtssiden `apps/` struktur verbum efter verbum og omfang efter omfang:"

# libretranslate
msgid "The subtree splits by user intent (the verb) and scope:"
msgstr "Undertræet splitter efter brugerens hensigt (verbet) og omfang:"

# libretranslate
msgid "The swarm deploy chain across both flavors:"
msgstr "Swarmkæden på tværs af begge varianter:"

# libretranslate
msgid "The swarm path applies the same cut through the `blocked` parameter of `applications_if_group_and_all_deps`; `disable` roles are cut from the dep walk, so orphaned providers never enter the provisioned inventory and `swarm_deploy_targets` (bounded by inventory presence) cannot re-add them."
msgstr "Den sværm sti anvender samme snit gennem `blocked` parameter `applications_if_group_and_all_deps`; `disable` roller er skåret fra dep walk, så forældreløse udbydere aldrig indtaste den provied inventar og `swarm_deploy_targets` (Begrænset af beholdningstilstedeværelse) kan ikke gen- tilføje dem."

# libretranslate
msgid "The swarm-test nfs-server serves shared storage from userspace `nfs-ganesha` (the `ganesha` flavor of `svc-storage-nfs-server`, the default in every runtime), which runs inside the privileged DinD node and never touches the host kernel `nfsd`, so an interrupted export cannot wedge the host. The `kernel` flavor is a per-inventory override for real hosts, where `nfsd` is not shared across clusters. If a swarm step ever hangs at `Reload NFS exports` from a stuck kernel-NFS mount, you MUST recover with `make swarm-clean` on the host (needs sudo): it removes what the docker CLI can, then runs `umount -f -l /var/lib/infinito` + `exportfs -ua` + `systemctl restart docker`. The no-sudo sandbox only prints those commands, so the host recovery is mandatory and the sweep MUST stop until it is done; never fall back to compose-only."
msgstr "Swarm- test nfs- serveren serverer delt opbevaring fra userspace `nfs-ganesha` (i `ganesha` smag af `svc-storage-nfs-server`, standard i hver runtime), som løber ind i den privilegerede DinD-knude og aldrig rører værtskernen `nfsd`, så en afbrudt eksport kan ikke kile værten. Den `kernel` smag er en per- inventar override for rigtige værter, hvor `nfsd` ikke deles på tværs af klynger. Hvis et sværm skridt nogensinde hænger på `Reload NFS exports` fra en fast kernel- NFS mount, skal du komme sig med `make swarm-clean` på værten (behov sudo): det fjerner hvad docker CLI kan, derefter kører `umount -f -l /var/lib/infinito` + `exportfs -ua` + `systemctl restart docker`. No- sudo sandkassen kun udskriver disse kommandoer, så værten opsving er obligatorisk og feje SKAL stoppe indtil det er gjort; aldrig falde tilbage til komponist-kun."

# libretranslate
msgid "The sweep's ordered candidate rows: priority line first, then the regular line, each annotated with the modes it offers and whether it is priority."
msgstr "Den feje bestilte kandidat rækker: prioritet linje først, derefter den almindelige linje, hver kommenteret med de tilstande, det tilbyder, og om det er prioritet."

# libretranslate
msgid "The sync pass is the whole disaster drill against the host this role deploys on (`BKP_TEST_IS_STACK_HOST`), in one sequence: back up, seed the marker, back up again so the tested generation carries it, take every project down, restore through the recover chain, require the marker and every recorded container back, and finally let the host's own container health service judge."
msgstr "Sync pass er hele katastrofen boret mod værten denne rolle anvender på (`BKP_TEST_IS_STACK_HOST`), i én sekvens: tilbage op, frø markøren, tilbage op igen, så den testede generation bærer det, tage hvert projekt ned, gendanne gennem gendannelseskæden, kræve markøren og hver registreret beholder tilbage, og endelig lade værtens egen container sundhedstjeneste dømme."

# libretranslate
msgid "The systemd services installed by `svc.sh` require a host with a real init system. Registration, service install, and service start are skipped when `DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER=true`; the role can be fully deployed in DinD (binary extraction and `.env` file work). The nested `deploy-fresh-purged-apps` call in `test.sh` is also skipped when `DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER=true` — in DinD, `make up` does not start the package-cache proxy (`cache_stack_enabled()` returns false in CI), so apt inside the fresh container cannot resolve the proxy hostname and package installs fail. Structural checks (binary + `.env`) are sufficient proof of a correct deploy in DinD; the full end-to-end deploy only runs on a real host."
msgstr "Systemd tjenester installeret af `svc.sh` kræver en vært med et rigtigt init-system. Registrering, service installation, og service start er sprunget, når `DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER=true`; rollen kan være fuldt indsat i DinD (binær ekstraktion og `.env` filarbejde). Den indlejrede `deploy-fresh-purged-apps` call in `test.sh` er også sprunget over når `DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER=true` - i DinD, `make up` ikke starter pakke- cache proxy (`cache_stack_enabled()` giver falsk i CI), så apt inde i den friske beholder kan ikke løse proxy værtsnavn og pakke installationer mislykkes. Strukturkontrol (binær + `.env`) er tilstrækkeligt bevis for en korrekt implementering i DinD; den fulde end-to-end implementering kun kører på en reel vært."

# libretranslate
msgid "The table below summarizes common Ansible plugin types and their conventional directory names."
msgstr "Tabellen nedenfor opsummerer fælles Ansible plugin typer og deres konventionelle mappenavne."

# libretranslate
msgid "The table lives in its own ``## Roles Overview 🧩`` section directly above ``## Use it online 🚀`` in the root README.md and is fully regenerated on every run; every other section stays untouched. Rows are the invokable roles, sorted ascending by the Entity column."
msgstr "Bordet lever i sin egen ``## Roles Overview 🧩`` sektion direkte ovenfor ``## Use it online 🚀`` i roden README.md og er fuldt regenereret på hver kørsel; hvert andet afsnit forbliver uberørt. Rækker er de usårlige roller, sorteret stigende af Kolonnen Enhed."

# libretranslate
msgid "The target path may be absolute or relative. Relative paths are interpreted relative to the current working directory, *not* the directory of the Path object."
msgstr "Målstien kan være absolut eller relativ. Relative stier fortolkes i forhold til den aktuelle arbejdsmappe, *ikke* mappen for kanal- objektet."

# libretranslate
msgid "The target refuses to drop a worktree with uncommitted changes. Show the operator that status and let them decide; only add `force=true` when they explicitly ask for it, because it discards the changes."
msgstr "Målet nægter at droppe et arbejdstræ med uforpligtende ændringer. Vis operatøren, at status, og lad dem beslutte; kun tilføje `force=true` når de udtrykkeligt beder om det, fordi det kasserer ændringerne."

# libretranslate
msgid "The target subtree must already exist; the script refuses to create export subtrees implicitly."
msgstr "Målet subtree skal allerede eksistere; scriptet nægter at skabe eksport subtrees implicit."

# libretranslate
msgid "The task sits in `tasks/stages/01_constructor.yml` after the `networks`, `design` and `service_provider` merges, after the `add_host` placements and after the token store, so the payload renders with the same `group_names`, `groups` and user records a role would see. Moving it earlier bakes stale values into the play."
msgstr "Opgaven ligger i `tasks/stages/01_constructor.yml` efter `networks`, `design` og `service_provider` Sammensmeltning, efter `add_host` placeringer og efter token butik, så nyttelasten gør med samme `group_names`, `groups` og bruger registrerer en rolle ville se. Flytte det tidligere bages gamle værdier ind i spillet."

# libretranslate
msgid "The template maps the generated palette to semantic variables such as `--color-01-solid-primary`, `--color-01-link-primary`, grayscale steps, and `--color-rgb-01-*`."
msgstr "Skabelonen kortlægger den genererede palette til semantiske variabler såsom `--color-01-solid-primary`, `--color-01-link-primary`, gråskala trin, og `--color-rgb-01-*`."

# libretranslate
msgid "The tested envelope 🧪"
msgstr "Den afprøvede konvolut 🧪"

# libretranslate
msgid "The theme MUST be bundled with the source repository (either checked in under ``themes/`` or referenced as a Hugo Module via ``go.mod``). V1 does not support a separate theme override."
msgstr "Temaet SKAL bundtes med kildelageret (enten checked in under ``themes/`` eller refereret som en Hugo Modul via ``go.mod``). V.1 understøtter ikke en separat overskrift."

# libretranslate
msgid "The theme MUST be bundled with the source repository (either checked in under `themes/` or referenced as a Hugo Module via `go.mod`). V1 does not support a separate theme override."
msgstr "Temaet SKAL bundtes med kildelageret (enten checked in under `themes/` eller refereret som en Hugo Modul via `go.mod`). V.1 understøtter ikke en separat overskrift."

# libretranslate
msgid "The three `API_*_KEY` entries are read as `${{ secrets.X || vars.X }}`, so a secret of the same name wins and the variable is the fallback. Prefer the secret: a repository **variable is not masked**, and the development inventory sets `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS: false`, so a key supplied as a variable can be printed by a task that echoes its own arguments."
msgstr "De tre `API_*_KEY` poster læses som `${{ secrets.X || vars.X }}`, Så en hemmelighed om det samme navn vinder, og variablen er fallback. Foretag hemmeligheden: et arkiv **variabel er ikke maskeret**, og udvikling inventar sæt `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS: false`, så en nøgle leveret som en variabel kan udskrives af en opgave, der afspejler sine egne argumenter."

# libretranslate
msgid "The three `svc-bkp-*` repository rows come from `backup_repos.repo_placements`. `utils/tests/swarm/matrix.py` calls `backup_repos.backup_provider_ips`, which resolves the same two closures and returns the nodes as IPs, to build `svc-bkp-remote-2-local.services.remote-2-local.backup_providers`."
msgstr "De tre `svc-bkp-*` depotrækker kommer fra `backup_repos.repo_placements`. `utils/tests/swarm/matrix.py` opkald `backup_repos.backup_provider_ips`, som løser de samme to lukninger og returnerer knudepunkterne som IPs, at opbygge `svc-bkp-remote-2-local.services.remote-2-local.backup_providers`."

# libretranslate
msgid "The three candidates that vendor documentation claimed were probed against running instances on 2026-08-27, and each is filed below on what the deployed artefact actually offers rather than on the claim:"
msgstr "De tre kandidater, som sælger dokumentation hævdede, blev undersøgt mod kørende tilfælde på 2026-08-27, og hver er indgivet nedenfor på, hvad den udsendte artefact faktisk tilbyder snarere end på kravet:"

# libretranslate
msgid "The title renders these as glyphs, so recovering one means translating a symbol back into a value; the log holds the word the operator picked. Reading it there keeps the retrigger honest even if the title's marker changes shape."
msgstr "Titlen gør disse som glyffer, så gendannelse en betyder at oversætte et symbol tilbage til en værdi; loggen holder det ord, operatøren valgte. Læsning af det der holder genudløser ærlig, selvom titlen markør ændrer form."

# libretranslate
msgid "The title's priority segment is the cross-check, not the source: it proves a priority line existed even when truncation mangled it, so an empty log read is a broken reader -- expired logs, a moved Inputs block, an inlined orchestrator -- rather than a run dispatched without one."
msgstr "Titlens prioriterede segment er krydstjekket, ikke kilden: det beviser, at der fandtes en prioritetslinje, selv når trunkationen lemlæstede den, så en tom log læse er en brudt læser -- udløbet logfiler, en flyttet Input blok, en inlined orkester -- snarere end et løb afsendt uden en."

# libretranslate
msgid "The token as an operator would have written it, for error messages."
msgstr "Tegn som en operatør ville have skrevet det, for fejlmeddelelser."

# libretranslate
msgid "The token can name a row this ranking no longer has -- the role was removed, a variant was dropped, the filters moved. The start is then the first row the source run got green, which lies inside the same window and so never falls behind it. A run with nothing green and an unresolvable token leaves no anchor at all and starts at the head."
msgstr "Tegnet kan navngive en række denne placering ikke længere har - rollen blev fjernet, en variant blev droppet, filtrene flyttet. Begyndelsen er så den første række kildeløbet fik grøn, som ligger inde i det samme vindue og så aldrig falder bag det. En løbetur med intet grønt og en uopløselig token efterlader overhovedet intet anker og starter i hovedet."

# libretranslate
msgid "The token each entry carries is the one the deployment issued, not the signed-in caller's own, so reaching an MCP tool server is a grant separate from signing in. The env renders `config.access_grants: []`, which `has_connection_access` reads as administrator-only, and [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) then narrows each entry to the serving role's `mcp` RBAC group."
msgstr "Den token hver post bærer er den implementering udstedt, ikke signeret-i opkaldsens egen, så nå en MCP værktøj server er et tilskud adskilt fra at logge ind. Env renders `config.access_grants: []`, som `has_connection_access` kun som administratorer, og [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) derefter indsnævrer hver indgang til serverrollen `mcp` RBAC-gruppen."

# libretranslate
msgid "The token each entry carries is the one the deployment issued, not the signed-in caller’s own, so reaching an MCP tool server is a grant separate from signing in. The env renders ``config.access_grants: []``, which ``has_connection_access`` reads as administrator-only, and ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ then narrows each entry to the serving role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "Den token hver post bærer er den implementering udstedt, ikke signeret-i opkaldsens egen, så nå en MCP værktøj server er et tilskud adskilt fra at logge ind. Env renders ``config.access_grants: []``, som ``has_connection_access`` kun som administratorer, og ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ then narrows each entry to the serving role’s ``mcp`` RBAC-gruppen."

# libretranslate
msgid "The token lifetime is bounded to one hour, and a new token is minted on every workflow run."
msgstr "Den symbolske levetid er afgrænset til en time, og en ny token er minded på hver workflow køre."

# libretranslate
msgid "The token lives in the store under the user named by the provider's ``mcp.credential.owner``, keyed by the provider's own ``application_id``. Spelling that out at each call site repeated the owner resolution, the two ``.get`` fallbacks and the trim in eighteen places, so a role that read it slightly differently read a different thing."
msgstr "Den token bor i butikken under brugeren navngivet af udbyderens ``mcp.credential.owner``, keyed af udbyderens egen ``application_id``. Stavning, der ud på hvert opkald sted gentaget ejerens opløsning, de to ``.get`` fallbacks og trim i atten steder, så en rolle, der læser det lidt anderledes læse en anden ting."

# libretranslate
msgid "The token owner; tool calls run with that account's Mattermost permissions"
msgstr "Den token ejer; værktøj opkald køre med denne konto Mattermost Tilladelser"

# libretranslate
msgid "The token owner; tool calls run with that account’s Mattermost permissions"
msgstr "Den token ejer; værktøj opkald køre med denne konto Mattermost Tilladelser"

# libretranslate
msgid "The token store at ``/var/lib/infinito/secrets/tokens.yml`` survives compose+volumes purges. Matrix-deploy variant transitions wipe an app's persistent state but the stale token would otherwise be reused on the next round (for example matomo's API probe in ``sys-front-inj-matomo``, whose token-empty guard never fires while the prior round's token is still present). The purge orchestrator invokes this module to drop the matching ``users.<user>.tokens.<app_id>`` entries alongside the entity-level wipe."
msgstr "Den token butik på ``/var/lib/infinito/secrets/tokens.yml`` Overlever komponere + mængder udrensninger. Matrix- implementere variant overgange tørre en app 's vedvarende tilstand, men den gamle token ville ellers blive genbrugt på næste runde (for eksempel matomos API sonde ind ``sys-front-inj-matomo``, Hvis vagt aldrig skyder, mens den forrige runde stadig er til stede). Den udrensning orkester påberåber dette modul til at droppe matchende ``users.<user>.tokens.<app_id>`` poster ved siden af entity- niveau tørre."

# libretranslate
msgid "The token store is written on `STACK_HOST` while every `lookup('users').tokens` reader executes on the Ansible controller. In compose the two are one machine; in swarm they are not, so a provider that mints and persists its credential still resolves to an empty bearer for every client. The store therefore has to reach the controller as well."
msgstr "Den token butik er skrevet på `STACK_HOST` hver `lookup('users').tokens` læser udfører på Ansible controller. I komponere de to er en maskine; i sværm de ikke er, så en udbyder, der mints og fortsætter sin kreditværdighed stadig løser til en tom bærer for hver klient. Butikken skal derfor også nå frem til kontrolløren."

# libretranslate
msgid "The top-level `compose.yml` is scoped to **local development and CI testing only**. It MUST NOT be used to deploy or run a live Infinito.Nexus stack. Production deployments MUST go through the Ansible roles and their own rendered compose files under `roles/<role>/templates/`."
msgstr "Top- niveau `compose.yml` er scoped til **kun lokal udvikling og CI-test**Det må ikke bruges til at implementere eller køre en live Infinito.Nexus stack. Produktions implementeringer SKAL gå gennem Ansible roller og deres egne afleveret komposition filer under `roles/<role>/templates/`."

# libretranslate
msgid "The top-level `env` block sets process environment variables for every Claude Code session. It is currently used to disable GPG signing for agent-created commits via the additive `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT` mechanism:"
msgstr "Top- niveau `env` Blok sæt proces miljøvariabler for hver Claude Code session. Det er i øjeblikket bruges til at deaktivere GPG signering for agent- oprettet tilsagn via tilsætningsstoffet `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT` mekanisme:"

# libretranslate
msgid "The top-level node MUST be a YAML list. A non-list root is a hard error."
msgstr "Top- niveau node SKAL være en YAML liste. En ikke- liste rod er en hård fejl."

# libretranslate
msgid "The trade-off is that `deny` now carries the full weight of \"what the agent must never do from the shell\". New destructive patterns MUST be added to `deny`. They can no longer be caught implicitly by an absent `allow` entry."
msgstr "Handel-off er, at `deny` Nu bærer den fulde vægt af \"Hvad agenten aldrig må gøre fra skallen\". Nye destruktive mønstre skal tilføjes til `deny`De kan ikke længere fanges implicit af en fraværende `allow` entry."

msgid "The transitive fields (``services`` / ``consumed_by`` and their counts) are the BFS closure capped at ``max_level``; the ``*_direct`` fields are always the one-hop neighbours. ``weight`` is the sum of the four numeric columns. ``dna`` is a hash of the role's own name unioned with its embedded services (sorted), so two roles covering the same service set share a dna. ``siblings`` are the other roles sharing that dna; ``clone`` is True for every row of a dna group except the heaviest one (ties broken by name), so sorting clones last keeps one representative per service set ahead of the budget cut. ``random`` is a per-row 6-digit nonce, rolled fresh per invocation, so tie order deliberately varies between runs. ``variant`` is the ``meta/variants.yml`` index this row was computed against, or ``None`` for a whole-role row. ``id`` and ``covered_by`` are set by the CLI after sorting: ``id`` is the row's numeric position in sort order (1-based), and ``covered_by`` is the ``id`` of the first earlier (green) row of a DIFFERENT role that embeds this row, or the sentinel ``0`` when this row is itself green (no real ``id`` is 0). Two variants of the same role never cover each other. ``row`` is the 1-based line number in the final rendered output (assigned last, after filtering), so it stays sequential even when sorting by ``covered_by`` scrambles ``id``. ``variants`` is the number of ``meta/variants.yml`` variants of the role in whole-role mode; under ``--variant`` each row already is a single variant, so it is ``1``. ``lifecycle`` is the role's ``meta/services.yml`` lifecycle stage (alpha/beta/pre/…). ``compose`` / ``swarm`` are True when the CI test-deploy matrix exercises the role in that mode, honouring the discovery skip logic: invokable + lifecycle in the tested envelope + the role's ``skip`` list. Under ``--variant`` ``swarm`` is per-variant (every variant deploys, so it tracks the role-level ``swarm`` and ``stack``). ``stack`` is True when the role renders its own container stack (ships a ``templates/*compose*.yml.j2``); host-only roles (backup, wireguard, swapfile) and pure service-injectors are False. ``swarm`` implies ``stack``: a role with no compose template of its own is never a swarm stack-deploy target, so ``swarm`` is forced False when ``stack`` is False. ``host`` mirrors the primary entity's ``modes.host.enabled`` flag (default True) for non-stack roles, and is forced False for a stack role: it marks invokable roles that configure the host instead of shipping a stack. ``test_compose`` / ``test_swarm`` / ``test_host`` duplicate the mode columns minus the role's ``meta/tests.yml`` ``skip`` list: ``modes`` states where a role RUNS, ``skip`` deactivates TESTING a mode, and CI discovery filters on these ``test_*`` columns. ``integrated`` is False when the row's direct service map keeps no foreign provider enabled (the role deploys isolated): per variant on variant rows, from the base ``meta/services.yml`` on whole-role rows."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "The translatable core strings are `galaxy_info.description` in every `roles/*/meta/main.yml` (266 roles), `title` and `description` of every node in [categories.yml](../../meta/categories.yml), the key and `description` of every entry in [menu_categories.yml](../../roles/web-app-dashboard/vars/menu_categories.yml), and the logout panel strings. Role titles are product names and MUST NOT be translated."
msgstr "De translaterbare kerne strenge er `galaxy_info.description` i `roles/*/meta/main.yml` (266 roller), `title` og `description` af hver knude i [categories.yml](../../meta/categories.yml), nøglen og `description` af hver indgang i [menu_categories.yml](../../roles/web-app-dashboard/vars/menu_categories.yml), og logout panel strenge. Rolletitler er produktnavne og må ikke oversættes."

# libretranslate
msgid "The translatable strings core ships, keyed by the ``msgctxt`` of their source."
msgstr "De translaterbare strenge kerne skibe, keyed af den ``msgctxt`` af deres kilde."

# libretranslate
msgid "The trigger is **group membership**, not a per-role flag."
msgstr "Triggeren er **gruppemedlemskab**, ikke et perrollemærke."

# libretranslate
msgid "The trivial static passthroughs live in two collector files: `passthrough.py` (always emitted) and `gha_passthrough.py` (emitted only when `ctx.on_gha` is true)."
msgstr "De trivielle statiske gennemgange lever i to samlerfiler: `passthrough.py` (altid udledt) og `gha_passthrough.py` (kun udsendt, når `ctx.on_gha` er sandt)."

# libretranslate
msgid "The trusted build additionally receives the Docker Hub mirror credentials (passed only when the label is present); untrusted builds mirror anonymously."
msgstr "Den betroede bygge derudover modtager Docker Hub spejl legitimation (bestået, når etiketten er til stede); Ubetroede bygger spejl anonymt."

# libretranslate
msgid "The two deploy-test workflows listed in the `Infrastructure tests` table of [workflows.md](../../tools/github/actions/workflows.md) (compose and swarm modes) run in parallel once DNS and mirroring have completed. Both cover all deployment types (`INFINITO_DISCOVER_ALL`, lifecycle-filtered to the `INFINITO_LIFECYCLES` envelope), not just the `web-*` server scope."
msgstr "De to arbejdsgange, der er anført i `Infrastructure tests` Tabel [workflows.md](../../tools/github/actions/workflows.md) (komponér og sværm tilstande) køre parallelt, når DNS og spejling har afsluttet. Begge dækker alle implementeringstyper (`INFINITO_DISCOVER_ALL`, lifecycle- filtreret til `INFINITO_LIFECYCLES` kuvert), ikke kun `web-*` serverskop."

# libretranslate
msgid "The two host-qualified forms, then the bare ``/`` for a target the upstream expressed as an absolute path."
msgstr "De to host- kvalificerede former, så den bare ``/`` for et mål opstrøms udtrykt som en absolut sti."

# libretranslate
msgid "The two inputs a retrigger decides itself rather than carrying over."
msgstr "De to input en genudløser beslutter sig i stedet for at overføre."

# libretranslate
msgid "The two measured inputs resolve in a fixed order: an inventory override (`RESOURCE_HOST_CPUS_OVERRIDE` / `RESOURCE_HOST_MEM_MB_OVERRIDE`), then the host's own hardware facts, then a probe of the machine this plugin runs on. The probe only applies to a target reached over the local connection, because a lookup executes on the Ansible controller: probing for a remote host would report the controller's hardware. That case raises and names the override to set."
msgstr "De to målte indgange forsvinder i en fast rækkefølge: en beholdningsoverskrift (`RESOURCE_HOST_CPUS_OVERRIDE` / `RESOURCE_HOST_MEM_MB_OVERRIDE`), så værtens egne hardware fakta, så en sonde af maskinen dette plugin kører på. Sonden gælder kun for et mål, der nås over den lokale forbindelse, fordi en opslag udfører på Ansible controller: sondering efter en fjernvært ville rapportere controllers hardware. Den sag hæver og nævner overriden, der skal sættes."

# libretranslate
msgid "The two mutual-exclusion guards (*tests/integration/iam/oauth2_oidc/test_mutual_exclusive.py*, *test_acl_mutual_exclusive.py*) — obsolete under the single-block schema."
msgstr "De to gensidige udelukkelsesvagter (*tests/integration/iam/oauth2_oidc/test_mutual_exclusive.py*, *test_acl_mutual_exclusive.py*) - forældet i henhold til et enkelt blokskema."

# libretranslate
msgid "The unified `# noqa` / `# nocheck` syntax that suppresses individual checks across the infinito-nexus test suite."
msgstr "Den `# noqa` / `# nocheck` syntaks, der undertrykker individuelle kontroller på tværs af infinito-nexus test suite."

# libretranslate
msgid "The unified schema supports:"
msgstr "Den samlede skema understøtter:"

# libretranslate
msgid "The universal-logout service ([web-svc-logout](../../../../../roles/web-svc-logout/)), when attached to a deployment, injects JavaScript that auto-detects every logout control across the role tree and rewrites it to redirect through Keycloak's end-session endpoint. Persona scenarios therefore do NOT branch on whether universal-logout is active: they always click the role's own logout button. The injected JS handles the redirect when active, the click clears the local session when not, and the post-click assertion (`assertUnauthenticatedLanding`) is identical in both cases."
msgstr "Universallogouttjenesten ([web-svc-logout](../../../../../roles/web-svc-logout/)), når de er knyttet til en implementering, indsætter JavaScript, der auto- detekterer hver logout kontrol på tværs af rolletræet og omskriver det til at omdirigere gennem KeycloakEndepunktet for slutsessionen. Persona scenarier derfor ikke gren om universallogout er aktiv: de altid klikke på rollens egen logout knap. Den injicerede JS håndterer omdiriger når aktiv, klik rydder den lokale session, når ikke, og post- klik påstand (`assertUnauthenticatedLanding`) er identisk i begge tilfælde."

# libretranslate
msgid "The upstream `oauth2-proxy` MUST set `X-Forwarded-User` (or `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`) and `X-Forwarded-Email` on every request that reaches the broker. Without `X-Forwarded-User`, the broker returns HTTP 401, there is no anonymous fallback by design."
msgstr "Opstrøms `oauth2-proxy` SKAL indstilles `X-Forwarded-User` (eller `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`) og `X-Forwarded-Email` på enhver anmodning, der når mægleren. Uden `X-Forwarded-User`, mægleren returnerer HTTP 401, der er ingen anonym fallback ved design."

# libretranslate
msgid "The upstream server is stdio-oriented and broadly mutating over a cache several applications share."
msgstr "Den opstrøms server er stdio- orienteret og stort set muterer over en cache flere applikationer deler."

# libretranslate
msgid "The upstream server is stdio-oriented and broadly mutating. Keep `stdio_only_and_shared_cache` unless an isolated instance, prefix-scoped ACL principal, pinned bridge, and exact read-only tool list are supplied. Prefer using Redis as an internal agent-memory backend rather than a user-visible server."
msgstr "Den opstrøms server er stdio- orienteret og stort set muterer. Behold `stdio_only_and_shared_cache` medmindre en isoleret instans, prefix- scoped ACL hovedstol, fastspændt bro, og nøjagtig read- only værktøj liste leveres. Foretrækker anvendelse Redis som en intern agent- memory motor snarere end en brugersynlig server."

# libretranslate
msgid "The user is a direct member of the expected group (not only a parent OU)."
msgstr "Brugeren er direkte medlem af den forventede gruppe (Ikke kun en modervirksomhed)."

# libretranslate
msgid "The user is created idempotently (safe to run multiple times)."
msgstr "Brugeren er skabt idempotently (sikker at køre flere gange)."

# libretranslate
msgid "The userland tools are baked into every distro image by [filesystem.sh](../../scripts/install/filesystem.sh); the kernel side comes from the host."
msgstr "De userland værktøjer er bagt ind i hver distro billede af [filesystem.sh](../../scripts/install/filesystem.sh)- Kernesiden kommer fra værten."

# libretranslate
msgid "The v3 address is ``base32(PUBKEY || CHECKSUM || VERSION)`` where ``CHECKSUM = SHA3-256(\".onion checksum\" || PUBKEY || VERSION)[:2]`` and ``VERSION = 0x03`` (see spec.torproject.org/address-spec). Tor stores the *expanded* ed25519 secret key ``clamp(SHA512(seed)[:32]) || SHA512(seed)[32:]`` in ``hs_ed25519_secret_key``; the public key ``clamp(SHA512(seed)[:32]) * B`` equals the standard ed25519 public key, so it is taken straight from ``cryptography`` without needing scalar multiplication."
msgstr "V3 adresse ``base32(PUBKEY || CHECKSUM || VERSION)`` hvor ``CHECKSUM = SHA3-256(\".onion checksum\" || PUBKEY || VERSION)[:2]`` og ``VERSION = 0x03`` (Se spec.torproject.org/ adresser- spec). Tor gemmer *udvidet* t25519 hemmelig nøgle ``clamp(SHA512(seed)[:32]) || SHA512(seed)[32:]`` til ``hs_ed25519_secret_key``; den offentlige nøgle ``clamp(SHA512(seed)[:32]) * B`` er25519 offentlig nøgle, så det er taget direkte fra ``cryptography`` uden behov for skalar multiplikation."

# libretranslate
msgid "The value a row draws from *pool* this sweep: a plain rotation over the row's global position, so consecutive rows spread across the pool and consecutive sweeps move every row on to the next value."
msgstr "Værdien en række trækker fra *pool* Denne feje: en almindelig rotation over rækken globale position, så fortløbende rækker spredt over poolen og fortløbende sweeps flytte hver række videre til næste værdi."

# libretranslate
msgid "The value as it now stands in the file, or \"\" when it was removed."
msgstr "Værdien som den nu står i filen, eller \"\" da det blev fjernet."

# libretranslate
msgid "The value can be adjusted or overridden via inventory, group vars, or host vars if needed."
msgstr "Værdien kan justeres eller tilsidesættes via inventar, gruppevars eller værtsvars, hvis det er nødvendigt."

# libretranslate
msgid "The value is always double-quoted in the output. That makes the emit safe for YAML edge cases like `restart: no` (bare `no` would otherwise parse as a boolean) without burdening the caller with quoting rules."
msgstr "Værdien er altid dobbelt-citeret i output. Det gør udløsningen sikker for YAML kant sager som `restart: no` (bare `no` ville ellers tolke som en boolean) uden at belaste den, der ringer, med at citere regler."

# libretranslate
msgid "The value must mirror how the backed-up group is keyed. `all` treats every matched run as one instance — correct for `global-ci-<repo>-<ref_name>`, which spans both `entry-push-latest.yml` and `entry-manual-steer.yml`, so a push must be able to reap a manual sweep. `event` keeps one instance per event name — correct for `pr-ci-<repo>-<event_name>-pr-<number>`. Grouping any finer than the real key spares a run the group would have reaped: per-workflow grouping leaves the manual sweep alive, because it is the newest run of its own workflow."
msgstr "Værdien skal afspejle, hvordan backed- up gruppen er rettet. `all` behandler hver matchede køre som én instans - korrekt `global-ci-<repo>-<ref_name>`, der spænder både `entry-push-latest.yml` og `entry-manual-steer.yml`, Så et skub skal kunne høste en manuel gennemsøgning. `event` holder én instans per begivenhed navn - korrekt for `pr-ci-<repo>-<event_name>-pr-<number>`. Gruppering nogen finere end den virkelige nøgle sparer en køre gruppen ville have høstet: per-workflow gruppering efterlader manuel feje levende, fordi det er den nyeste køre af sin egen arbejdsgang."

# libretranslate
msgid "The values one axis may draw from this run."
msgstr "De værdier, en akse kan trække fra denne kørsel."

# libretranslate
msgid "The variant of *app* that carries the replay, and the mode it runs in."
msgstr "Varianten af *app* som bærer replay, og den tilstand det kører i."

# libretranslate
msgid "The variant only affects inventory generation; the Ansible deploy itself reads `applications.<app>` overrides from the variant-resolved inventory and MUST NOT consult variant data at runtime."
msgstr "Varianten påvirker kun lagerproduktion; Ansible deployering selv læser `applications.<app>` override fra variant- løst opgørelse og SKAL IKKE konsultere variantdata ved runtime."

# libretranslate
msgid "The variant override is baked as a real boolean into the inventory, so the shared-service auto-include picks it up at build time. Variant 0 therefore pulls `web-app-discourse` into the include set. Variant 1 does not."
msgstr "Variantoverriden er bagt som en rigtig boolesk ind i inventaret, så shared- service auto- omfatter samler det op på byggetid. Variant 0 derfor trækker `web-app-discourse` ind i inklusion sæt. Variant 1 - Nej."

# libretranslate
msgid "The variant that enables the fewest services, as the matrix writes it; the lowest index wins a tie, and ``''`` means none qualifies."
msgstr "Den variant, der gør det muligt for de færreste tjenester, som matrix skriver det; det laveste indeks vinder et slips, og ``''`` betyder ingen kvalificering."

# libretranslate
msgid "The verb folder name expresses the deploy intent. The script name expresses the scope."
msgstr "Det verbum mappe navn udtrykker deployering hensigt. Scriptnavnet udtrykker omfanget."

# libretranslate
msgid "The version is read from roles/<application_id>/files/package-lock.json, so the URL is always the exact pinned, lockfile-reproducible version."
msgstr "Versionen er læst fra roller /<application_id>/ filer / emballage -lock.json, så webadressen er altid den nøjagtige fastlåst, lockfile- reproducerbar version."

# libretranslate
msgid "The vhost is identified by the ``domains.canonical`` key that carries the domain, which is the same key ``server.status_codes`` uses. A domain that is not canonical, or a key that declares nothing, falls back to the declared ``default``."
msgstr "Vhost er identificeret af ``domains.canonical`` nøgle der bærer domænet, som er den samme nøgle ``server.status_codes`` anvendelser. Et domæne, der ikke er kanonisk, eller en nøgle, der ikke erklærer noget, falder tilbage til den erklærede ``default``."

# libretranslate
msgid "The vocabulary a package plan is written in."
msgstr "Ordforråd en pakkeplan er skrevet i."

# libretranslate
msgid "The volume repo contributes a database step after its file steps: the dumps have to land once the volumes are back and while the consumers are still down, which is where the caller has them."
msgstr "Volumen repo bidrager med en database trin efter dens fil trin: lossepladser er nødt til at lande, når mængderne er tilbage, og mens forbrugerne er stadig ned, hvilket er, hvor den, der ringer, har dem."

# libretranslate
msgid "The warning MUST name the role, the addon id, and the failing step so the operator can act without reading raw task output."
msgstr "Advarslen SKAL angive rollen, addon id, og det svigtende trin, så operatøren kan handle uden at læse rå opgave output."

# libretranslate
msgid "The wget half stays proxy-aware on purpose: busybox wget rejects ``--proxy=off``, and this flavor exists for images where which tool ships is unknown, so hardening it there would break the very case it covers."
msgstr "Wget halvdel forbliver proxy- bevidst med vilje: busybox wget afviser ``--proxy=off``, og denne smag eksisterer for billeder, hvor hvilket værktøj skibe er ukendt, så hærdning det der ville bryde selve sagen det dækker."

msgid "The wildcard in the namespace slot collapses 21 mutating verbs across `gh issue/pr/release/repo/ruleset/run/cache/gist/label/project/…` into a single rule per verb. Future namespaces that ship the same verb (e.g. a hypothetical `gh discussion lock`) are caught automatically. Explicit per-namespace lists rot as the `gh` CLI grows."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "The window's start is the floor: with nothing green behind it the answer is the start itself, never the head. Walking back to the head is what made every retrigger redeploy the whole stretch its predecessors had already proven."
msgstr "Vinduets start er gulvet: Med intet grønt bag det er svaret selve starten, aldrig hovedet. At gå tilbage til hovedet er det, der fik alle genudløser til at genindsætte hele den strækning, dens forgængere allerede havde bevist."

# libretranslate
msgid "The wiring block sits behind a ``file_exists`` guard on ``extensions/VisualEditorPlus/vendor/autoload.php``, because ``LocalSettings.php`` is rendered before the extensions are installed and ``VisualEditorPlus`` fatals until its composer step has run."
msgstr "Ledningerne blok sidder bag en ``file_exists`` Vagt på ``extensions/VisualEditorPlus/vendor/autoload.php``, fordi ``LocalSettings.php`` leveres før udvidelser er installeret og ``VisualEditorPlus`` fatale indtil dens komponisttrin er kørt."

# libretranslate
msgid "The wiring block sits behind a `file_exists` guard on `extensions/VisualEditorPlus/vendor/autoload.php`, because `LocalSettings.php` is rendered before the extensions are installed and `VisualEditorPlus` fatals until its composer step has run."
msgstr "Ledningerne blok sidder bag en `file_exists` Vagt på `extensions/VisualEditorPlus/vendor/autoload.php`, fordi `LocalSettings.php` leveres før udvidelser er installeret og `VisualEditorPlus` fatale indtil dens komponisttrin er kørt."

# libretranslate
msgid "The wiring that makes this work is purely in the `services` declaration, not in `run_after`:"
msgstr "De ledninger, der gør dette arbejde er udelukkende i `services` erklæring, ikke i `run_after`:"

# libretranslate
msgid "The workaround used here is the **GitLab OAuth2 provider** (`MM_GITLABSETTINGS_*`), which is generic enough to work with any OIDC-compatible identity provider including Keycloak. This provides true SSO: user accounts are automatically created in Mattermost on first login."
msgstr "Det arbejde, der anvendes her er **GitLab OAuth2 udbyder** (`MM_GITLABSETTINGS_*`), som er generisk nok til at arbejde med enhver OIDC- kompatibel identitet udbyder, herunder KeycloakDette giver ægte SSO: brugerkonti oprettes automatisk i Mattermost på første login."

# libretranslate
msgid "The workaround used here is the **GitLab OAuth2 provider** (``MM_GITLABSETTINGS_*``), which is generic enough to work with any OIDC-compatible identity provider including Keycloak. This provides true SSO: user accounts are automatically created in Mattermost on first login."
msgstr "Det arbejde, der anvendes her er **GitLab OAuth2 udbyder** (``MM_GITLABSETTINGS_*``), som er generisk nok til at arbejde med enhver OIDC- kompatibel identitet udbyder, herunder KeycloakDette giver ægte SSO: brugerkonti oprettes automatisk i Mattermost på første login."

# libretranslate
msgid "The workflow-driven jobs additionally require the `BOT_APP_CLIENT_ID` and `BOT_APP_PRIVATE_KEY` repository secrets, see [secrets.md](secrets.md). Without those secrets, runs fail at the token-minting step and no PR is opened."
msgstr "De workflowdrevne job kræver desuden `BOT_APP_CLIENT_ID` og `BOT_APP_PRIVATE_KEY` arkivhemmeligheder, se [secrets.md](secrets.md). Uden disse hemmeligheder, kører fejle på tappetrin og ingen PR åbnes."

# libretranslate
msgid "The workload form only changes step 6: a stack that carries services gets `docker stack rm`, a role whose compose renders none gets its compose project stopped on every node. `has_swarm_service` decides by asking the deployed stack. Every other step operates on volumes, the NFS export and the deployed backup units, independent of the orchestrator."
msgstr "Arbejdsbyrden form kun ændrer trin 6: en stak, der udfører tjenester får `docker stack rm`, en rolle, hvis sammensætning gør ingen får sin sammensætning projekt stoppet på hver node. `has_swarm_service` beslutter ved at spørge den indsatte stak. Hvert andet skridt opererer på mængder, NFS eksport og de udsendte backup enheder, uafhængigt af orkester."

# libretranslate
msgid "The worst entry point (``entry-*.yml``) adds its own jobs to the same run before calling the orchestrator; that overhead is subtracted too."
msgstr "Det værste indgangssted (``entry-*.yml``) tilføjer sine egne job til samme løb, før du ringer til orkester; at overhead er trukket også."

# libretranslate
