msgid "These are deployment-orchestration failures, not playwright-parity failures, and were therefore deferred per the autonomy escape clause (archived req 019)."
msgstr "Der er tale om deployment-orkestrering fiaskoer, ikke playwright-paritet fiaskoer, og blev derfor udsat pr autonomiundtagelsesklausulen (arkiveret req 019)."

# libretranslate
msgid "These are desktop GNOME Shell extensions with no in-app web surface to drive, so they are exempt from the Playwright requirement (requirement 026, Decision 11)."
msgstr "Disse er desktop GNOME Shell udvidelser med ingen in-app web overflade til at køre, så de er fritaget fra Playwright krav (krav 026, afgørelse 11)."

# libretranslate
msgid "These are optional and fail soft: unset means the provider's route is never published, and the deployment falls back to whatever local backend the round deploys. The workflow reads each as `${{ secrets.X || vars.X }}`, so the same name works as a repository variable; see [configuration.md](configuration.md#provider-keys-variable-or-secret-) for why the secret is the better half of that pair."
msgstr "Disse er valgfrie og mislykkes bløde: frakoblet betyder, at udbyderens rute aldrig bliver offentliggjort, og indsættelsen falder tilbage til, hvad den lokale bagende den runde rammer. Arbejdsgangen lyder hver som `${{ secrets.X || vars.X }}`, så det samme navn fungerer som en depotvariabel; se [configuration.md](configuration.md#provider-keys-variable-or-secret-) For hvorfor hemmeligheden er den bedre halvdel af det par."

# libretranslate
msgid "These are used only for pulling source images from Docker Hub and are not required for GHCR authentication."
msgstr "Disse bruges kun til at trække kildebilleder fra Docker Hub og er ikke nødvendige for GHCR godkendelse."

# libretranslate
msgid "These assets are meant to support confidence, not ceremony. They help the project validate real-world behavior across local development, CI environments, and deployment-oriented smoke tests. The emphasis is on practical feedback: when something breaks, the surrounding test tooling should make the failure easier to understand, easier to reproduce, and easier to clean up. 🚀"
msgstr "Disse aktiver er beregnet til at støtte tillid, ikke ceremoni. De hjælper projektet validere real-world adfærd på tværs af lokal udvikling, CI miljøer, og deployment-orienterede røgtest. Der lægges vægt på praktisk feedback: Når noget går i stykker, bør det omgivende testværktøj gøre fejlen lettere at forstå, lettere at reproducere og lettere at rydde op. 🚀"

# libretranslate
msgid "These build on the working onion node and are implemented after the web core is verified."
msgstr "Disse bygger på den arbejdende løg node og er implementeret efter web-kernen er verificeret."

# libretranslate
msgid "These choices are settled at requirement creation time and bound the implementation. Re-opening any of them MUST be recorded in the implementing PR."
msgstr "Disse valg er afgjort på krav oprettelse tid og bundet gennemførelsen. Genåbning af en af dem skal registreres i den implementerende PR."

# libretranslate
msgid "These decisions were confirmed by the operator before implementation starts and are NOT subject to re-litigation during implementation."
msgstr "Disse beslutninger blev bekræftet af operatøren, inden gennemførelsen påbegyndes, og er IKKE genstand for genbehandling under gennemførelsen."

# libretranslate
msgid "These have genuine forks and MUST be resolved with the operator before or during implementation. Do not silently pick one and bury it."
msgstr "Disse har ægte gafler og SKAL løses med operatøren før eller under gennemførelsen. Vælg ikke en stille og begrav den."

# libretranslate
msgid "These operations are unconditionally blocked, regardless of any `allow` entry or sandbox state. They cover destructive patterns whose blast radius is unacceptable even inside the sandbox (`.` is `allowWrite`, so `rm -rf .` would still erase the working tree and `.git/`)."
msgstr "Disse operationer er betingelsesløst blokeret, uanset om `allow` entry or sandbox state. De dækker destruktive mønstre, hvis sprængradius er uacceptabel selv inde i sandkassen. (`.` er `allowWrite`, så `rm -rf .` ville stadig slette det arbejdende træ og `.git/`)."

# libretranslate
msgid "These operations pause and require explicit operator approval before executing, even when sandboxed."
msgstr "Disse operationer pause og kræver udtrykkelig operatørgodkendelse før udførelse, selv når sandkassen."

# libretranslate
msgid "These package definitions are required to bootstrap and run the local development/test environment reliably. 🚀"
msgstr "Disse pakkedefinitioner er nødvendige for at bootstrap og køre den lokale udvikling / test miljø pålideligt. 🚀"

# libretranslate
msgid "These pages drill into a single workflow rather than enumerate every target. `make help` is the authoritative list of available targets:"
msgstr "Disse sider borer ind i en enkelt arbejdsgang i stedet for at opregne hvert mål. `make help` er den autoritative liste over tilgængelige mål:"

# libretranslate
msgid "These permissions are required for DNS record management, CAA/SPF/DKIM handling, cache purging, and certificate provisioning."
msgstr "Disse tilladelser er nødvendige for DNS record management, CAA/SPF/DKIM håndtering, cache udrensning, og certifikat levering."

# libretranslate
msgid "These primitives are entity-keyed. The app-keyed orchestrator [apps.sh](../apps.sh) maps app ids to entities and drives them in sequence alongside the token-store wipe in [tokens.py](../../../../utils/cleanup/tokens.py)."
msgstr "Disse primitive er retskaffede. Den udvalgte orkester [apps.sh](../apps.sh) Kort app-id 'er til enheder og kører dem i rækkefølge sammen med plus- store tørre i [tokens.py](../../../../utils/cleanup/tokens.py)."

# libretranslate
msgid "These principles govern how teams collaborate, plan, and deliver work. For code design principles, see [principles.md](../design/principles.md)."
msgstr "Disse principper regulerer, hvordan teams samarbejder, planlægger og udfører arbejde. For så vidt angår kodedesignprincipper, se [principles.md](../design/principles.md)."

# libretranslate
msgid "These roles remain out of shared MCP discovery. A future exception requires a new requirement with a fixed operation list, dedicated identity, isolation boundary, human approval for mutations, and audit trail."
msgstr "Disse roller forbliver uden for delt MCP opdagelse. En fremtidig undtagelse kræver et nyt krav med en fast operationsliste, dedikeret identitet, isolationsgrænse, menneskelig godkendelse af mutationer og revisionsspor."

# libretranslate
msgid "These rules are enforced via branch protection. See [branch.md](artefact/git/branch.md) for the full policy."
msgstr "Disse regler håndhæves via filialbeskyttelse. Se [branch.md](artefact/git/branch.md) for hele politikken."

# libretranslate
msgid "These rules keep shared role values explicit, reusable, and easy to read."
msgstr "Disse regler holder delte rolleværdier eksplicitte, genanvendelige og let at læse."

# libretranslate
msgid "These scripts are the SPOT for repository identity resolution."
msgstr "Disse scripts er SPOT for arkividentitetsopløsning."

# libretranslate
msgid "These scripts keep PR scope detection, branch-prefix validation, and fork merge-ref resolution together in one place. The `🧩 Subset` label's PR-body parser lives in the `cli.meta.ci.subset_roles` module; the dispatcher [pr_affected_roles.sh](../../../github/resolve/pr_affected_roles.sh) selects between it and the diff resolver. See the \"Subset label\" section in [pipeline.md](../../../../docs/contributing/artefact/git/pipeline.md)."
msgstr "Disse scripts holder PR scope detektion, branch- prefix validering, og gaffel merge- ref opløsning sammen på ét sted. Den `🧩 Subset` mærkets PR- body parser bor i `cli.meta.ci.subset_roles` modul; afsenderen [pr_affected_roles.sh](../../../github/resolve/pr_affected_roles.sh) vælger mellem det og diff- løsningen. Se \"Undersæt etiket\" Section in [pipeline.md](../../../../docs/contributing/artefact/git/pipeline.md)."

# libretranslate
msgid "These scripts run **on the deployed host**, not on the controller. `test-e2e-cli` renders `templates/test.env.j2` into the environment and calls `test.sh`, which orchestrates the rest. They use `systemctl`, the `container` wrapper and `/etc/machine-id`, so they only make sense where the role actually deployed."
msgstr "Disse scripts køre **om den udsendte vært**, ikke på controlleren. `test-e2e-cli` automater `templates/test.env.j2` ind i miljøet og opkald `test.sh`, som arrangerer resten. De bruger `systemctl`, `container` papir og `/etc/machine-id`, så de kun giver mening, hvor den rolle faktisk indsat."

# libretranslate
msgid "These scripts run inside the local infinito container and remove container-local state only. For the canonical Make target index that invokes these helpers, see [make.md](../../../docs/contributing/tools/make.md)."
msgstr "Disse scripts kører inde i den lokale infinito container og fjerne container- lokale stat. For den kanoniske Make mål indeks, der påkalder disse hjælpere, se [make.md](../../../docs/contributing/tools/make.md)."

# libretranslate
msgid "These steps are the shared repository workflow and apply regardless of whether you work on Linux, macOS, or Windows with WSL2."
msgstr "Disse trin er det delte arkiv arbejdsgang og gælder, uanset om du arbejder på Linux, macOS eller Windows med WSL2."

# libretranslate
msgid "These templates are intended for inclusion in larger NGINX configuration files via Jinja2.   They modularize your configuration by separating HTML, WebSocket, and media proxying, allowing for clear, reusable, and maintainable reverse proxy logic."
msgstr "Disse skabeloner er beregnet til optagelse i større NGINX konfigurationsfiler via Jinja2. De modularisere din konfiguration ved at adskille HTML, WebSocket, og medier proxy, der giver mulighed for klar, genanvendelig, og mainreable reverse proxy logik."

# libretranslate
msgid "These variables cap the `infinito` container so local runs can reproduce GitHub-hosted runner pressure. Each default is `0`, which Docker interprets as \"unlimited\" and is identical to omitting the key. See [ci.md](../../actions/debugging/ci.md) for runner specs and reproduction profiles."
msgstr "Disse variable grænser `infinito` container, så lokale løb kan reproducere GitHub-hostede runner pres. Hver standard er `0`, som Docker fortolker som \"unlimited\" og er identisk med at udelade nøglen. Se [ci.md](../../actions/debugging/ci.md) for runner specs og reproduktionsprofiler."

# libretranslate
msgid "They are also the rows a run must not sample. A priority row is deployed in **every combination it can take** — each variant, in each mode its role offers, and on the modes that carry the onion axis once behind Tor and once on clearnet — all within the same sweep. A 3-variant role offering compose and swarm therefore becomes 3 × 2 × 2 = **12 jobs**, not 3. That is the point of naming a role in `priority`: it is proven everywhere at once instead of over four sweeps."
msgstr "Det er også de rækker, en løbetur ikke må udtage. En prioriteret række er indsat i **hver kombination det kan tage** - hver variant, i hver tilstand dens rolle tilbyder, og på de tilstande, der bærer løg akse én gang bag Tor og én gang på clearnet - alle inden for samme sweep. A 3-variant rolle tilbyder komposition og sværm derfor bliver 3 × 2 × 2 = **12 job**, ikke 3Det er meningen med at nævne en rolle i `priority`: det er bevist overalt på én gang i stedet for over fire sweeps."

# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "They live at ``meta/services.yml.<primary_entity>.{run_after,lifecycle}`` where ``<primary_entity>`` is the value returned by :func:`utils.roles.entity.name.get_entity_name` for the role's directory name."
msgstr "De bor på ``meta/services.yml.<primary_entity>.{run_after,lifecycle}`` hvor ``<primary_entity>`` er den værdi, der returneres af :func:`utils.roles.entity.name.get_entity_name` for rollens mappenavn."

# libretranslate
msgid "They live at ``secrets.credentials``, which is where the roles' own vars and every other consumer address them. Reading the top-level ``credentials`` instead returns nothing for every provider whose ``credential.source`` is ``credentials``, and the deploy then aborts on a secret that was provisioned all along."
msgstr "De bor på ``secrets.credentials``, Det er her rollernes egne varevogne og alle andre forbrugere henvender sig til dem. Læsning af topniveau ``credentials`` i stedet returnerer intet for hver udbyder, hvis ``credential.source`` er ``credentials``Og så aborterer deployeringen på en hemmelighed, der blev leveret hele tiden."

# libretranslate
msgid "They must not contain application-specific configuration values."
msgstr "De må ikke indeholde anvendelsesspecifikke konfigurationsværdier."

# libretranslate
msgid "They should be listed as Idle in ``github.com/<owner>/infinito-nexus/settings/actions/runners``."
msgstr "De bør være opført som tomgang i ``github.com/<owner>/infinito-nexus/settings/actions/runners``."

# libretranslate
msgid "They should be listed as Idle in `github.com/<owner>/infinito-nexus/settings/actions/runners`."
msgstr "De bør være opført som tomgang i `github.com/<owner>/infinito-nexus/settings/actions/runners`."

# libretranslate
msgid "They travel as `INFINITO_API_OPENAI_KEY`, `INFINITO_API_ANTHROPIC_KEY` and `INFINITO_API_OPENROUTER_KEY` through the workflow `env:` block, the passthrough allowlist in [passthrough.py](../../../../../utils/env/handlers/passthrough.py), the `infinito` service environment in [compose.yml](../../../../../compose.yml), and land in `API.<provider>.api_key` in the development inventory, whose path is the SPOT behind `INFINITO_INVENTORY_VARS_FILE`. Skipping the compose forwarding makes them resolve to empty inside the container without any error."
msgstr "De rejser som `INFINITO_API_OPENAI_KEY`, `INFINITO_API_ANTHROPIC_KEY` og `INFINITO_API_OPENROUTER_KEY` gennem arbejdsgangen `env:` blokken, adgangskort i [passthrough.py](../../../../../utils/env/handlers/passthrough.py), `infinito` servicemiljø i [compose.yml](../../../../../compose.yml), og land i `API.<provider>.api_key` i udviklingsoversigten, hvis sti er SPOT bag `INFINITO_INVENTORY_VARS_FILE`. Skippe komponenten videresendelse gør dem løse at tømme inde i beholderen uden nogen fejl."

# libretranslate
msgid "Thin orchestrator that defines `EnvBuilder`, `BuildContext`, and `build_env()`. Walks the handler registry."
msgstr "Tynde orkester, der definerer `EnvBuilder`, `BuildContext`, og `build_env()`. Går efter den kontaktperson register."

# libretranslate
msgid "Thin orchestrator: each variable's mapping/computation lives in its own module under :mod:`utils.env.handlers`. ``build_env`` walks the ``ORDERED_HANDLERS`` registry, letting each handler read/write through an :class:`EnvBuilder`."
msgstr "Tynde orkester: hver variabel kortlægning / beregning lever i sit eget modul under :mod:`utils.env.handlers`. ``build_env`` går den ``ORDERED_HANDLERS`` Register, der lader hver kontakt læse / skrive gennem en :class:`EnvBuilder`."

# libretranslate
msgid "Thin wrapper around the `image` lookup (the SPOT for resolving the ``<registry>/<image>:<version>`` reference). ``container_image`` only adds the ``image: \"...\"`` compose-line wrapping so templates can drop it in as a standalone statement:"
msgstr "Tynde wrapper omkring `image` lookup (SPOT til løsning af ``<registry>/<image>:<version>`` reference). ``container_image`` kun tilføjer ``image: \"...\"`` compose- line indpakning, så skabeloner kan droppe det i som en selvstændig erklæring:"

# libretranslate
msgid "Third render backend (additive)"
msgstr "Tredje retribut- motor (Tilsætningsstof)"

# libretranslate
msgid "This **Infinito.Nexus Presentation** is a tool designed for showcasing the Infinito.Nexus platform to various audiences, including **Administrators**, **Developers**, **End-Users**, **Businesses**, and **Investors**. The presentation leverages **Reveal.js** to create an interactive, engaging, and fully containerized experience that can be easily deployed with Docker."
msgstr "Dette **Infinito.Nexus Presentation** er et værktøj designet til fremvisning af Infinito.Nexus platform til forskellige målgrupper, herunder **Administratorer**, **Udviklere**, **Slutbrugere**, **Virksomheder**, og **Investorer**. Præsentationen udtrækker **Reveal.js** at skabe en interaktiv, engagerende og fuldt containeriseret oplevelse, der nemt kan anvendes med Docker."

# libretranslate
msgid "This 3-node topology (1 manager + 2 workers) is also the minimum exercised by the CI pilot workflow — see [CI: pilot validation workflow](#ci-pilot-validation-workflow). Any host in `svc-swarm-manager` MUST also be in `svc-swarm-node`. A deploy with a host in `svc-swarm-manager` but missing from `svc-swarm-node` MUST fail at inventory-validation time."
msgstr "Dette 3-node topologi (1 manager + 2 arbejdstagere) er også det minimum, der udøves af CI pilot workflow - se [CI: pilotvalideringsarbejdsgang](#ci-pilot-validation-workflow). Enhver vært i `svc-swarm-manager` Skal også være i `svc-swarm-node`. En mission med en vært i `svc-swarm-manager` men mangler fra `svc-swarm-node` SKAL fejle på opfinder- valideringstid."

# libretranslate
msgid "This Ansible role automates the installation and configuration of [Certbot](https://certbot.eff.org/), a free and open-source tool for automating the deployment of [Let's Encrypt](https://letsencrypt.org/) certificates. It also handles the setup of DNS plugins for ACME challenges."
msgstr "Denne Ansible rolle automatiserer installation og konfiguration af [Certbot](https://certbot.eff.org/), et gratis og open source værktøj til automatisering af deployering af [Lad os kryptere](https://letsencrypt.org/) certifikater. Det håndterer også opsætningen af DNS plugins til ACME udfordringer."

# libretranslate
msgid "This Ansible role automates the installation and configuration of `Certbot <https://certbot.eff.org/>`__, a free and open-source tool for automating the deployment of `Let’s Encrypt <https://letsencrypt.org/>`__ certificates. It also handles the setup of DNS plugins for ACME challenges."
msgstr "Denne Ansible rolle automatiserer installation og konfiguration af `Certbot <https://certbot.eff.org/>`__, et gratis og open source værktøj til automatisering af deployering af `Let’s Encrypt <https://letsencrypt.org/>`__ certifikater. Det håndterer også opsætningen af DNS plugins til ACME udfordringer."

# libretranslate
msgid "This Ansible role automates the integration of Matomo tracking code into NGINX-served websites. It simplifies the process of adding the Matomo analytics tracking script and image tracker to all your web pages served through NGINX."
msgstr "Denne rolle automatiserer integrationen af Matomo spore kode til NGINX- serverede hjemmesider. Det forenkler processen med at tilføje Matomo analytics tracking script og billede tracker til alle dine websider serveret gennem NGINX."

# libretranslate
msgid "This Ansible role automates the validation of [Content Security Policy (CSP)](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CSP) enforcement for all configured domains by crawling them using a [CSP Checker](https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/csp-checker)."
msgstr "Denne Ansible rolle automatiserer valideringen af [Indhold Sikkerhedspolitik (CSP)](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CSP) håndhævelse for alle konfigurerede domæner ved at kravle dem ved hjælp af en [CSP- kontrol](https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/csp-checker)."

# libretranslate
msgid "This Ansible role automates the validation of `Content Security Policy (CSP) <https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CSP>`__ enforcement for all configured domains by crawling them using a `CSP Checker <https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/csp-checker>`__."
msgstr "Denne Ansible rolle automatiserer valideringen af `Content Security Policy (CSP) <https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CSP>`__ håndhævelse for alle konfigurerede domæner ved at kravle dem ved hjælp af en `CSP Checker <https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/csp-checker>`__."

# libretranslate
msgid "This Ansible role automatically restarts Docker Compose configurations with exited or unhealthy containers on Arch Linux systems. It ensures the stability of containerized workloads by recovering from common error conditions like port binding issues."
msgstr "Denne Ansible rolle genstarter automatisk Docker Compose konfigurationer med udstødte eller usunde beholdere på Arch Linux-systemer. Det sikrer stabiliteten af containererede arbejdsbelastninger ved at komme sig fra almindelige fejltilstande som portbindende problemer."

# libretranslate
msgid "This Ansible role configures NGINX to perform 301 redirects from one domain to another. It handles SSL certificate retrieval for the source domains and sets up the NGINX configuration to redirect to the specified target domains."
msgstr "Denne Ansible rolle Downloader NGINX til at udføre 301 omdirigerer fra et domæne til et andet. Det håndterer SSL certifikat hentning for kildedomænerne og opretter NGINX konfiguration til at omdirigere til de angivne måldomæner."

# libretranslate
msgid "This Ansible role configures the OpenSSH daemon (``sshd``) by deploying a templated ``sshd_config`` file. It applies secure, best-practice settings to harden remote access and reduce the risk of misconfiguration or lockout. Settings include disabling root login, enforcing public-key authentication, and setting appropriate logging levels."
msgstr "Denne Ansible rolle er OpenSSH dæmonen (``sshd``) ved at indsætte en templated ``sshd_config`` fil. Det gælder sikre, best-praksis indstillinger til at hærde fjernadgang og reducere risikoen for forkert konfiguration eller lockout. Indstillinger omfatter deaktivering af root login, håndhævelse af offentlig-nøgle autentificering, og indstilling af passende logningsniveauer."

# libretranslate
msgid "This Ansible role configures the OpenSSH daemon (`sshd`) by deploying a templated `sshd_config` file. It applies secure, best-practice settings to harden remote access and reduce the risk of misconfiguration or lockout. Settings include disabling root login, enforcing public-key authentication, and setting appropriate logging levels."
msgstr "Denne Ansible rolle er OpenSSH dæmonen (`sshd`) ved at indsætte en templated `sshd_config` fil. Det gælder sikre, best-praksis indstillinger til at hærde fjernadgang og reducere risikoen for forkert konfiguration eller lockout. Indstillinger omfatter deaktivering af root login, håndhævelse af offentlig-nøgle autentificering, og indstilling af passende logningsniveauer."

# libretranslate
msgid "This Ansible role deploys **NGINX** as a high-performance [reverse proxy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reverse_proxy) in front of Docker-hosted services.   It provides automatic TLS integration, WebSocket support, and a flexible templating system for per-application configuration."
msgstr "Denne ansible rolle **NGINX** som en høj ydeevne [reverse proxy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reverse_proxy) foran Docker- hostede tjenester. Det giver automatisk TLS integration, WebSocket support, og et fleksibelt templating system til per- applikation konfiguration."

# libretranslate
msgid "This Ansible role deploys **NGINX** as a high-performance `reverse proxy <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reverse_proxy>`__ in front of Docker-hosted services."
msgstr "Denne ansible rolle **NGINX** som en høj ydeevne `reverse proxy <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reverse_proxy>`__ foran Docker- hostede tjenester."

# libretranslate
msgid "This Ansible role deploys Collabora Online (CODE) in Docker to enable real-time, in-browser document editing for Nextcloud. It automates the setup of the Collabora CODE container, NGINX reverse proxy configuration, network isolation via Docker networks, and environment variable management."
msgstr "Denne ansible rolle Collabora Online (KODE) i Docker for at aktivere real- time, in- browser dokumentredigering for NextcloudDet automatiserer opsætningen af Collabora CODE container, NGINX reverse proxy konfiguration, netværk isolation via Docker netværk, og miljø variabel styring."

