# libretranslate
msgid "This role does NOT configure OIDC against ``web-app-keycloak``, LDAP against ``svc-db-openldap``, or any role-claim / LDAP-group RBAC mapping. Bridgy Fed authenticates users via their fediverse or atproto credentials at the source platform, not via local accounts. There is no local user table to bind an external IdP to, and no in-app authorisation tier to map a Keycloak role or LDAP group onto. Placing Bridgy Fed behind ``web-app-keycloak``\\ ’s SSO-proxy sidecar would break inbound federation traffic and MUST NOT be done. This SSO and RBAC exception is documented per `lifecycle.md <../../docs/contributing/design/role/services/lifecycle.md>`__."
msgstr "Denne rolle konfigurerer IKKE OIDC mod ``web-app-keycloak``, LDAP mod ``svc-db-openldap``, eller enhver role- claim / LDAP-gruppe RBAC mapping. Bridgy Fed autentificerer brugere via deres fediverse eller atproto legitimation på kilden platform, ikke via lokale konti. Der er ingen lokal brugertabel at binde en ekstern IdP til, og ingen in-app godkendelse niveau til at kortlægge en Keycloak rolle eller LDAP gruppe til. Placering Bridgy Fed bag ``web-app-keycloak``\\ 's SSO- proxy sidevogn ville bryde ind føderation trafik og SKAL IKKE gøres. Denne SSO og RBAC undtagelse er dokumenteret pr `lifecycle.md <../../docs/contributing/design/role/services/lifecycle.md>`__."

