# libretranslate
msgid "When the log carries the matrix-deploy round/pass markers, the result is segmented (one block of records per variant round + pass). Otherwise a single combined block is returned. Runtime rows are read from the ``ROLES RECAP`` sections only (never ``TASKS RECAP``, whose role-less task rows would double-count); a log without any recap header falls back to reading every profile-shaped line. The recap ``total`` line survives as the ``total`` row so consumers can cross-check the parsed sum. Per-host task results (``ok:``, ``changed:``, ``skipping:``, ``fatal:``, ``failed:`` under a ``TASK [role : ...]`` header) accumulate into each record's ``hosts`` field; delegation targets (``[host -> other]``) count for the source host. Raises FileNotFoundError when the log is absent (the caller turns that into a hard failure)."
msgstr "Når loggen bærer matrix- deployering runde / pass markører, er resultatet segmenteret (én records pr. variant runde + pass). Ellers returneres en enkelt samlet blok. Runtime rækker læses fra ``ROLES RECAP`` Kun dele (aldrig ``TASKS RECAP``, hvis role- mindre opgave rækker ville fordoble-tælle); en log uden nogen recap header falder tilbage til at læse hver profileformet linje. Genoptag ``total`` linje overlever som ``total`` række, så forbrugerne kan krydstjekke den fortolkede sum. Per- vært opgaveresultater (``ok:``, ``changed:``, ``skipping:``, ``fatal:``, ``failed:`` under a ``TASK [role : ...]`` header) akkumuleres i hver records ``hosts`` område; delegationsmål (``[host -> other]``) tælle for kilden vært. Øger FileNotFoundError, når loggen er fraværende (Den, der ringer, bliver en hård fiasko.)."

# libretranslate
msgid "When the oauth2-proxy SSO flavor is active, Snipe-IT’s native ``loginViaRemoteUser()`` is enabled via the ``Setting`` model (``login_remote_user_enabled``, ``login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME``). nginx gates ``/login`` through oauth2-proxy/Keycloak and injects the verified ``X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`` header, which Snipe-IT matches against ``users.username`` (the user must pre-exist and be activated — sync them via LDAP) to mint a native ``snipeit_session``. Visitors without a matching activated user silently fall through to the normal login form (no error). The password/LDAP login form stays available as a fallback (``login_common_disabled = 0``), and the in-app logout is redirected to the central OIDC end-session URL."
msgstr "Når oauth2-proxy SSO smag er aktiv, Snipe- IT 's indfødte ``loginViaRemoteUser()`` er aktiveret via ``Setting`` model (``login_remote_user_enabled``, ``login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME``). nginx porte ``/login`` gennem oauth2- proxy /Keycloak og injicerer den verificerede ``X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`` header, som Snipe- IT matcher mod ``users.username`` (brugeren skal præeksistere og aktiveres - synkronisere dem via LDAP) at male en indfødt ``snipeit_session``. Besøgende uden en matchende aktiveret bruger lydløst falde igennem til den normale login form (ingen fejl). Adgangskoden / LDAP login formular forbliver tilgængelig som en fallback (``login_common_disabled = 0``), og in- app logout er omdirigeret til den centrale OIDC end- session URL."

