# libretranslate
msgid "[x] Flowise 3.1.4 is reconciled through `/api/v1/custom-mcp-servers`, registers only Streamable HTTP providers, stores headers encrypted, authorizes each entry, and verifies exact tool names and schemas. The reconciler refuses to register a provider whose declared transport is not the one the role declares, stores the bearer as a `CUSTOM_HEADERS` `authConfig` Flowise encrypts at rest, and authorizes every entry. Name verification was vacuous until now, because the desired entry hardcoded an empty tool list; it compares against the provider's declared allowlist. The schema half is enforced where the schema contract lives: the adapter serving those tools pins `tools.schema_sha256` and calls `policy.assert_no_drift` at startup, so a changed schema fails the provider rather than being re-checked from a client that cannot see the contract file."
msgstr "[x] Flowise 3.1.4 er forsonet gennem `/api/v1/custom-mcp-servers`, registrerer kun Streamable HTTP-udbydere, gemmer overskrifter krypteret, autoriserer hver indgang, og verificerer nøjagtige værktøjsnavne og skemaer. Samtaler nægter at registrere en udbyder, hvis erklærede transport ikke er den, rollen erklærer, oplagrer bæreren som en `CUSTOM_HEADERS` `authConfig` Flowise krypterer i hvile, og autoriserer hver indgang. Navnekontrollen var upræcis indtil nu, fordi den ønskede indgang hardkodede en tom værktøjsliste; den sammenligner med udbyderens erklærede allolist. Skemaet halvdelen håndhæves, hvor skema kontrakt bor: adapteren betjener disse værktøjer pins `tools.schema_sha256` og opkald `policy.assert_no_drift` ved opstart, så en ændret skema mislykkes udbyderen snarere end at blive genkontrolleret fra en klient, der ikke kan se kontrakten fil."

# libretranslate
msgid "[x] Flowise Streamable HTTP support remains blocked or bridged until a pinned source-audited release passes an end-to-end tool call. The source audit of `flowise@3.1.4` settles it: `MCPToolkit.initialize` connects a `StreamableHTTPClientTransport` first and falls back to `SSEClientTransport` only when that connection throws, so the `'sse'` literal the registry service passes selects \"not stdio\" rather than a transport. The role's own module docstring claimed the opposite, that only SSE providers could be registered, while `meta/mcp.yml` declared `streamable_http`; the docstring was the wrong half and is corrected. The end-to-end tool call is the managed Agentflow fixture, which the deploy executes and fails on."
msgstr "[x] Flowise Strømbar HTTP-understøttelse forbliver blokeret eller begrænset, indtil en fast kilde- revideret udgivelse passerer et end-to-end værktøj opkald. Kilderevisionen af `flowise@3.1.4` afgør det: `MCPToolkit.initialize` forbinder en `StreamableHTTPClientTransport` først og falder tilbage til `SSEClientTransport` Kun når forbindelsen kaster, så `'sse'` bogstavelig Register Service passerer vælger \"ikke stdio\" I stedet for en transport. Rollens egen modul docstring hævdede det modsatte, at kun SSE udbydere kunne registreres, mens `meta/mcp.yml` anmeldt `streamable_http`; docstring var den forkerte halvdel og er rettet. Ende- to- end tool call er den administrerede Agentflow stativ, som deployeringen udfører og mislykkes på."

