# libretranslate
msgid "`INFINITO_CACHE_PACKAGE_MAX_AGE_MIN` (default `8640` = 6 days) controls how long every Nexus proxy repo holds an upstream response before revalidating. The bootstrap helper applies it as `contentMaxAge`, `metadataMaxAge`, and `negativeCache.timeToLive`. The default is intentionally one day below the 7-day `Valid-Until` window Debian and Ubuntu generate in their apt `Release` files, so Nexus always refreshes the manifest before `apt-get update` would see it expired. Raise it for slow-moving upstreams when staleness is preferable to upstream load; lower it further for fast-moving feeds (`apt-debian-security`, branch-pinned tarballs) when staleness becomes visible."
msgstr "`INFINITO_CACHE_PACKAGE_MAX_AGE_MIN` (standard `8640` = 6 dage) kontrollerer, hvor længe hver Nexus proxy repo holder en opstrøms respons, før den genvalideres. Bootstrap hjælper anvender det som `contentMaxAge`, `metadataMaxAge`, og `negativeCache.timeToLive`. Standard er med vilje en dag under 7- dag `Valid-Until` vindue Debian og Ubuntu genererer i deres apt `Release` filer, så Nexus altid genopfrisker manifestet før `apt-get update` ville se det udløbet. Hæv den for langsomme opstrøms når stilheden er at foretrække frem for opstrøms belastning; sænk den yderligere for hurtige feeds (`apt-debian-security`, forgrenede tarballs) når stilheden bliver synlig."

