# libretranslate
msgid "`KEEP_NEWEST_PER` — keeps the newest run of each group instance alive and cancels only the older ones, which is the rule the concurrency group itself applies. It is what makes the fallback safe against races: the head SHA from the event payload goes stale while the job waits for a runner, and a `[skip ci]` or `GITHUB_TOKEN` push moves the branch tip without creating a run at all. Selecting by \"not the current head\" would then cancel the newest commit's CI and spare the stale one, or leave the branch with no CI at all. Selecting by \"not the newest run\" cannot, in any ordering."
msgstr "`KEEP_NEWEST_PER` - holder den nyeste køre af hver gruppe instans i live og annullerer kun de ældre, hvilket er reglen concurrent gruppe selv gælder. Det er, hvad der gør fallback sikker mod racer: hovedet SHA fra begivenheden nyttelasten går skævt, mens jobbet venter på en runner, og en `[skip ci]` eller `GITHUB_TOKEN` skubbe flytter grenspidsen uden at skabe en køre overhovedet. Valg ved \"ikke det aktuelle hoved\" vil derefter annullere den nyeste commit 's CI og spare den gamle en, eller forlade grenen uden CI overhovedet. Valg ved \"ikke den nyeste kørsel\" kan ikke, i nogen bestilling."

# libretranslate
